"Blood Altar",
"Break a blood altar teleport tablet. It teleports the player to the ruins.",
"Use Drakan's medallion to teleport to the Meiyerditch Laboratories, then go through the tunnels to the ruins.",
"To save a charge on Drakan's medallion, the player may teleport to Morytania with the ectophial first. The medallion can be used to bank at Burgh de Rott bank. Blood Rune Temple is considered to be outside of Morytania which means teleporting via the medallion within it will consume charges, so it is advised to either exit the altar first or recharge the medallion at Burgh de Rott. However, the cost of congealed blood used to charge the medallion is negligible and it is much easier to use charges and recharge the medallion later.",
"Without Drakan's medallion, the Blood Rune Temple can be accessed through the Meiyerditch laboratory from its various entrances, the easiest access coming from the trapdoor behind the Hair of the Dog tavern in Canifis. Enter the cavern containing the tomb of Ivandis and take the other exit. This route is not commonly used by runecrafters as it is much slower than the other options.",
"without catalytic anima stones",
"Carapace",
"Crafting clockwork",
"Money making guide/Crafting clockwork",
"8 Crafting",
"25 Construction",
"40 Magic",
"Clockwork",
"Use the spell House Teleport (no rune cost with 50 Construction, or if using the Abyssal Link relic).",
"Use War's Retreat Teleport.",
"This article assumes the Lodestone Network is used to teleport to the Taverley lodestone and enter the player-owned house there (House Teleport can be used with 40 Magic, it is faster but consume runes), and a Beast of Burden is not used. Banking can be done via various teleportation methods (e.g. ring of duelling, or a mounted amulet of glory in the Quest Hall requiring 47 Construction). Each trip can be done within 2 minutes (30 trips an hour assumed).",
"Alternatively, if you have access to the Ithell district and an attuned crystal teleport seed, you can teleport to the Ithell district bank chest directly and then move east to the nearby POH portal.",
"Start out at the TzHaar Fight Cave bank in TzHaar City. Unload pure essence and store it in your pouches, then take out essence for your inventory. Run north and use the fairy ring to teleport to Zanaris. From there, run south to the agility shortcut -- if you have 66 Agility, go through both of them, although you may get stuck and take a small amount of damage before passing through. Run further south and enter the mysterious ruins, and then go directly to the altar. Craft your essence in your inventory and pouches, and then teleport back to the Fight Cave with your TokKul-Zo. If you are unwilling or unable to complete The Elder Kiln to gain the TokKul-Zo, it is possible to use the Wilderness Sword, starting at the Edgeville Bank and running across the river to the fairy ring there. This method is likely to be a little less efficient.",
"Break a cosmic altar teleport tablet. It teleports the player to the ruins.",
"Use any fairy ring or a portable fairy ring to teleport to Zanaris and go south to the ruins. There are jutting walls that can be traversed with level 46 or 66 Agility to get to the ruins faster.",
"Zanaris",
"At realistic speed, you can do 90 trips to the Cosmic Altar via the Abyss per hour, using the Wilderness sword to teleport back to Edgeville while using the powerburst of sorcery every fourth trip. It also assumes that the player has Wilderness Elite tasks completed for increased magical thread chance.",
"With optimised dives and surges, one can expect around 112–138 trips an hour, while without using any mobility abilities, one can expect 90–105 trips an hour.",
"The Mage of Zamorak is located in low-level wilderness, near the source of the River Lum. Make sure PvP is toggled off at Vala in Edgeville. The suggested outfit is as follows (make sure enhanced excalibur has the Mobile perk and the Wilderness sword is in the inventory).",
"65 Runecrafting",
"MOURNINGS_END_PART_2",
"The Mage of Zamorak is located low-level wilderness, near the source of the River Lum. Make sure PvP is toggled off by talking to Vala in Edgeville. See Abyss for more information on how to navigate the abyss.",
"Death Altar",
"Break a death altar teleport tablet. It teleports the player to the ruins.",
"The Tirannwn quiver 3 or 4 can teleport to the ruins 5 times a day.",
"Entering the ruins by walking requires entering the Temple of Light and using the following directions.",
"Go up the stairs at the main entrance.",
"The Tirannwn quiver 3 gives 5 free teleports to the Death altar each day. Start at a bank and fill your essence pouches, as well as ethereal body and familiar if you have them. Activate your Tirannwn quiver 3 and use keybind 5 to teleport to the death altar, enter and craft your runes. Teleport back to a bank and repeat another 4 times. This method can be combined with the use of the free teleports from the Wicked hood to get extended use out of your summoning familiar, however, it is generally more profitable to craft other runes with those teleports, see Wicked hood.",
"After buying the required soft clay, use a portable crafter to craft any type of unfired decorated urns with a brooch of the gods equipped. As two clay are required per urn, a Beast of Burden such as a Pack Yak can be used to carry additional clay. The portable crafter should be placed so that it can be used without moving from a bank.",
"After all the unfired urns are created, you can now begin firing them using the Fire urn spell from the Lunar spellbook. An Elemental battlestaff can cover the cost of the elemental runes, which only leaves the astral runes that need to be procured. For both steps (crafting and firing), bank presets are highly recommended. Once the portable crafter has been used once, any further crafting in the area will gain the bonus without needing to click the portable again.",
"The time taken to craft and bank is about 64 seconds for 28 rings.",
"The Artisan's outfit is a bonus experience set as a reward from Stealing Creation costing 100 reward points per piece. Each item alone provides 1% more Crafting experience when worn. When all of the set is equipped, the total bonus increases to 6%.",
"New Foundations recommended (needed to access Fort Forinthry - alternatively, anywhere with a close bank and furnace, eg. Falador, Lumbridge, Edgeville)",
"Deposit the gold bars into the metal bank at the furnace. Create a bank preset with an inventory filled with 28 dragonstones. Run to the furnace and use it to craft an inventory of dragonstone bracelets. Run back to bank, reload your preset and repeat.",
"Deposit the gold bars into the metal bank at the furnace. Create a bank preset with an inventory filled with 28 dragonstones. Run to the furnace and use it to craft an inventory of dragonstone necklaces. Run back to bank, reload your preset and repeat.",
"Deposit the gold bars into the metal bank at the furnace. Create a bank preset with an inventory filled with 28 dragonstones. Run to the furnace and use it to craft an inventory of dragonstone rings. Run back to bank, reload your preset and repeat.",
"Deposit the gold bars into the metal bank at the furnace. Create a bank preset with an inventory filled with 28 dragonstones. Run to the furnace and use it to craft an inventory of dragonstone amulets (unstrung). Run back to bank, reload your preset and repeat.",
