"In addition, the vast majority of their drops are noted or otherwise stackable, allowing for long trips. They are located in the Mos Le'Harmless Caves, access to which requires completion of Cabin Fever. Players also need a light source and a witchwood icon to avoid taking a great deal of damage. The easiest ways to get to the caves are taking the fairy ring DIP (requires A Fairy Tale III - Battle at Ork's Rift), or taking Bill Teach's boat from Port Phasmatys to Mos Le'Harmless, then travelling east from the town.",
"The easiest way to get to the dungeon is by teleporting to Lumbridge, going into the castle basement with a light source, and enter the swamp caves by the entrance next to Mistag. Head south and west, avoiding wall beasts, until you reach an area with three cave slime. Consult for more details. Be careful of gas in the caves, as if you have an open light source (i.e. torch, oil lamp, etc.) the gas will explode dealing high damage and extinguishing your light source. A bullseye lantern or similar is recommended.",
"Celestial Dragons can be accessed by catching the boat from the line ghost captain with his rowing boat, just north of the Port Phasmatys bank. The trip is free, arriving at the radiant wisp colony. From there, the Dragontooth Island resource dungeon is a short distance South. Players with a Hoardstalker ring or Dungeoneering cape can teleport directly to the resource dungeon.",
"Staff",
