"With an Ardougne cloak, the unicows have a chance of dropping noted unicorn horns instead, saving inventory space. Due to an update, this noted effect is permanently enabled and there is no way to disable it in order to guaranteed un-noted drops. However noted unicorn horn can be un-noted one at a time by either a right-click option on the Altar, or 'use' the horn on the Altar. With one unicorn horn and a war tortoise and inventory full of cowhides, it is possible to create and kill up to 45 unicows per trip. This will usually generate about 90 unicorn horns. Banking may be done via the fairy ring (code DJP). Returning to the Tower of Life may be done via the fairy ring once more or using the Ardougne cloak teleport to the Kandarin Monastery. Six or more trips per hour are feasible.",
"Tower of Life (building)",
"Ardougne",
"The fastest way to get to vinecrawlers is to use the fairy ring BJS, which must first be unlocked by using 5 bittercap mushrooms on it. Otherwise the player will have to run west of the incandescent wisp colony to enter the grove.",
"Snape grass seed",
"Prayer potion (3)",
"Looting Shifting Tombs",
"Money making guide/Looting Shifting Tombs",
"90 Agility",
"90 Thieving",
"90 Crafting",
"90 Prayer",
"Bladed Dive (recommended)",
"Off-hand khopesh of the Kharidian",
"Your profit rate may be higher or lower depending on speed.",
"To maximize tombs per hour, players should be prepared to teleport out instead of getting to the exit rope if the pathing is unfavorable. The best method for resetting at shifting tombs are as follows from best to worst.",
"Soul talisman",
"Toadflax potion (unfinished)",
"82 Herblore",
"Making botanist's amulets",
"Money making guide/Making botanist's amulets",
"Amulet mould (if not already in your tool belt)",
"Artisan's outfit",
"The botanist's amulet is in high demand because when the amulet is worn, there is approximately a 5% chance to brew a 4-dose potion instead of a 3-dose potion while training Herblore. As Herblore is one of the most expensive skills to train, the amulet provides a good way of saving gp and increasing total dosages.",
"The final step in this method is to enchant the amulets by using the Lvl-2 Enchant spell in Standard spells. Wield a Staff of air to save the air rune cost.",
"Edgeville or Combat academy bank",
"Greater",
"20 Necromancy",
"To find the current location of a Portable well, ask in the \"portables\" Friends chat.",
"Crafting Guild",
"Eternal plank",
"The first location for red sandstone is just outside of Oo'glog. This location can be mined for 50 sand stone a day and is right near the Robust glass machine. Mine a full inventory and then crawl through the adjacent hole into Oo'glog. Run west to the robust glass machine and left click it to convert all your red sandstone to robust glass. After that, blow the glass into flasks and then bank them. Return to the rock outside of Oo'glog and mine the rest of your daily red sandstone, turning those into flasks as well.",
"102 Herblore",
"112 Herblore",
"90 Herblore",
"Making refined planks at Fort Forinthry",
"Money making guide/Making refined planks at Fort Forinthry",
"Assumes the guide's 576 actions per hour. Adjust it to your own pace.",
"Making ritual candles",
"Money making guide/Making ritual candles",
"Repeat with the listed supplies; the finished candles are stackable.",
"Flamtaer",
"With a good internet connection and fast banking, up to 2400 potions/hr is not uncommon. A tick-perfect execution would have 3000 potions/hr (and some more due to the scroll of cleansing's effect), but that is hard to achieve due to the difficulty of banking without losing potion-making ticks.",
"Please note that the portable well 10% extra chance to duplicate a potion does not apply to combination potions. As such, the only cost-saving boosts are the modified botanist mask and the scroll of cleansing.",
"The experience rate assumes the usage of a portable well, maximum potency torstol incense sticks, maximum advanced pulse core boost, and the maximum clan avatar boost.",
"Use a teak eagle lectern or mahogany eagle lectern in the Study of the player-owned house to make Ardougne teleports. A servant (recommended butler or better) can be used to bring soft clay to you to remove the need for banking, and with 60 invention, a Mind-controlled monkey butler can be used to forgo the need to pay for the butler trips. Any staff that provides water runes is required to save the cost of the water runes, such as a Staff of water. Using a Law staff with water runes may be more profitable depending on rune prices.",
"Use a mahogany eagle lectern in the Study of the player-owned house to make Heart teleports. A servant (recommended butler or better) can be used to bring soft clay to you to remove the need for banking, and with 60 invention, a Mind-controlled monkey butler can be used to forgo the need to pay for the butler trips. Any staff that provides fire runes is required to save the cost of the fire runes, such as a Staff of fire.",
"Use a mahogany eagle lectern in the Study of the player-owned house to make Watchtower teleports. A servant (recommended butler or better) can be used to bring soft clay to you to remove the need for banking, and with 60 invention, a Mind-controlled monkey butler can be used to forgo the need to pay for the butler trips. An Elemental battlestaff is required to save both air and earth runes.",
"Use an eagle lectern, teak eagle lectern, or mahogany eagle lectern in the Study of the player-owned house to make Lumbridge teleports. A servant (recommended butler or better) can be used to bring soft clay to you to remove the need for banking, and with 60 invention, a Mind-controlled monkey butler can be used to forgo the need to pay for the butler trips. An Elemental battlestaff is required to save both air and earth runes.",
"Use a mahogany eagle lectern in the Study of the player-owned house to make north-western anachronia teleports. A servant (recommended butler or better) can be used to bring soft clay to you to remove the need for banking, and with 60 invention, a Mind-controlled monkey butler can be used to forgo the need to pay for the butler trips.",
"Use any lectern in the Study of the player-owned house to make Varrock teleports. A servant (recommended butler or better) can be used to bring soft clay to remove the need for banking, and with 60 invention, a Mind-controlled monkey butler can be used to forgo the need to pay for the butler trips. An Elemental battlestaff is required to save both air and fire runes.",
"Use a mahogany eagle lectern in the Study of the player-owned house to make Watchtower teleports. A servant (recommended butler or better) can be used to bring soft clay to you to remove the need for banking, and with 60 invention, a Mind-controlled monkey butler can be used to forgo the need to pay for the butler trips. Any staff that provides earth runes is required to save the cost of the earth runes, such as a Staff of earth.",
"Spirit weed potion (unfinished)",
"When you have all your supplies, head to world 84 Fort Forinthry if you're not using your own portable wells. It is possible to further boost your potions made per hour by using a beast of burden such as a pack yak along with presets.",
"After all your potions are made, head to any decanting NPC such as War in War's Retreat or Bob Barter (herbs) in the Grand Exchange and have him decant your super saradomin brew (3) into super saradomin brew flasks.",
"Irit potion (unfinished)",
"Kwuarm potion (unfinished)",
"Compost bins; Manor Farm is one option",
"There is usually a portable well placed and maintained by someone else next to the bank chest in the Lumbridge Market in world 84. However, if there isn't one and no-one else provides one within a reasonable amount of time, you may have to use your own wells. With a Portable Well, you can expect to produce approximately 2,310 Spirit weed potion (unfinished) per hour.",
"WATCHTOWER",
"Cave nightshade",
"The easiest way to get there is by teleporting to the Yanille lodestone and walking to the most northern cave entrance marked on the map to the right. A skavid map is required to enter. A light source is required to prevent damage from swarming insects. Armoured gloves are required to pick cave nightshades. Cave nightshades can be noted with magic notepaper by using the nightshade on the paper, but not vice versa. Signs of the porter may also be used to bank the harvest.",
"Varrock south-east mine",
"Pickaxe of earth and song with Honed 6 and Refined 4",
"Elder rune ore box if not using signs of the porter",
"This is an excellent way to mine fairly AFK for a long period of time, and the metamorphic geode does provide some additional income over time, but it is highly dependent on luck and having the Refined perk. Alternatively, the player can use the Fortune perk to occasionally mine an extra ore. Stone spirit and ore prices fluctuate significantly on the Grand Exchange, so be sure to test prices before heavily investing in materials. For a close approximation of ore mined per hour (of pure mining) based on your levels and gear, see the mining rate calculator.",
"A grace of the elves allows Seren spirits to spawn, which reward the player with an item from the rare drop table. It can also be charged with signs of the porter to bank items. However, be aware that the grace of the elves has a high upfront cost as it becomes permanently untradeable once equipped for the first time.",
"A grace of the elves allows Seren spirits to spawn and reward the player with an item from the rare drop table. It can also be charged with signs of the porter to bank items. However, be aware that the grace of the elves has a sunk cost as it becomes permanently untradeable once equipped for the first time.",
"80 Mining",
"Banite ore",
"Wilderness (level 54) Pirates' Hideout mine",
"Clay is an item that is always in demand due to soft clay being used in Crafting. There are many locations to mine clay, but one of the best locations is in the Burthorpe mines, located southwest of the bank. Once you have a full inventory, leave the mines and deposit your clay at the bank.",
"Teleport directly to the Burthorpe lodestone.",
"Teleport to the Taverley lodestone or use the House Teleport spell to the Taverley POH portal (if the player has a house there) and walk north.",
"Teleport to the Troll Invasion Distraction and Diversion by using the games necklace.",
"Teleport just outside the Warriors' Guild by using the combat bracelet.",
"Free-to-play can either teleport close to a bank and run back via the Al Kharid lodestone or run to and from the Het's Oasis bank.",
"Necronium pickaxe + 4 or better",
"Use Dungeoneering cape teleport to the Dwarven Mine resource dungeon and then running north and west to the cavern entrance.",
"Through a directed skill portal in the Max Guild of Prifddinas. Requires Plague's End and at least one 99 or a Quest Cape.",
"Use the Lassar Teleport from the Ancient Magicks spellbook, the Edgeville Monastery teleport from the combat bracelet, or the Body altar teleport all teleport close to this entrance of the Dwarven Mine. Then run south to the cavern entrance.",
"Through the entrance in the north-east corner of Falador or the Mining Guild and then run north and then west to the entrance to the Living Rock Caverns.",
"Adamant ore box or better",
"Gold ore can be mined from concentrated gold deposits in the Living Rock Caverns. Concentrated gold deposits yield five gold ores at once unlike normal gold rocks. There are , but it is recommended to use the two southern spawns that are closest to the bank deposit which is located in the centre of the cavern.",
"Copper ore",
"Mining iron ore",
"Money making guide/Mining iron ore",
"Iron ore box or better",
"Everything Is Oresome",
"Mining iron ore can be done in many places throughout Gielinor, but for Free to play, one of the best is within the Dwarven mines underneath Falador, at the Dwarven iron mine. It's recommended to have at least 15 Dungeoneering as this allows access to the Dwarven mine resource dungeon which has a bank deposit inside, drastically decreasing the time it takes to bank. To obtain 1,914 iron ore an hour, you will need to maintain full stamina and be using iron stone spirits.",
"You also get sedimentary geodes while mining. They can be opened later to retrieve spirit shards and different gems. Players should use the best pickaxe available to them, as each pickaxe upgrade increases the amount of xp and ore gained. For a close approximation of ore mined per hour (of pure mining) based on your levels and gear see the mining rate calculator.",
"Dwarven mines; use the iron rock area described in the guide",
"Varrock armour 1 (recommended)",
"Honed 6 and Fortune recommended",
"spell",
"With the release of Fort Forinthry, limestone has gone up in price. The limestone mine that is most easily accessible is the Silvarea quarry, which can be reached rather quickly with the Skeletal horror Teleport or the invitation box. Mining the limestone rock once around half-way through each backpack to keep mining stamina high to maintain maximum mining speed. Craft your full backpack of limestone into limestone bricks. There is a deposit box close by, south, next to Maria, since limestone does not store in an ore box.",
"Dwarven mine",
"Mithril ore",
"Mining mithril ore can be done in several places but one of the best places to mine mithril ore is in the Dwarven mines underneath Falador. Going down the stairs in the house east of the party room and then entering the mysterious entrance which is located west of the stairs. Level 15 Dungeoneering is required to enter the mysterious entrance. Once entered you'll see a bank deposit box with a mithril rock right next to it. Click the rock and start mining, when you have a full inventory, deposit the ore into the bank deposit box and then click the rock again to start the process again. It should take around 1 second to bank and start mining again. It should be noted that you will be getting sedimentary geodes while mining, which can be opened later to retrieve spirit shards and gems. The player should use the best pickaxe possible as it will grant more ores per hour.",
"Magic golem outfit or the lesser golem outfits",
"Necrite ore",
"Phasmatite",
"75 Summoning",
"Primal pickaxe + 5 at minimum for best rates",
"Augmented pickaxe of life and death recommended with Honed 6 and Refined 4 perks",
"Marmaros ore",
"Mining red and crystal sandstone",
"Money making guide/Mining red and crystal sandstone",
"Glassblowing pipe stored on the toolbelt",
"Collector's insignia for additional yield",
"Artificer's measure for additional yield",
"Grace of the elves and Luck of the Dwarves for seren spirits",
"50 recommended for waterfiend",
"Augmented pickaxe with Honed 6 and Fortune 3 for additional yield",
"The above output is assuming 110 Mining, 110 Strength, and using a primal pickaxe + 5.",
"Run to the nearby robust glass machine and create 28 crystal glass.",
"99 Mining",
"Varrock Set Tasks - Elite for Varrock armour 4",
"Elder rune pickaxe + 5",
"Bracelet of clay",
"It is recommended to do this while Voice of Seren is active in the Ithell district as the hour's effect allows a 50% chance that each soft clay will be transported directly to the player's bank. It is recommended to use bracelets of clay which doubles the amount of clay received. Within the Ithell district there is a nearby bank chest, pottery wheel, and pottery oven that can be used to craft.",
"42 Archaeology",
"Tin ore",
"Level 92 Farming is required to raise dragons and have royal dragons in the large pens. Each pile of red dragon manure can be mucked to fill one bucket. Climb into the stile, hover over a pile of red dragon manure, and click \"Muck out Dragon manure\" to fill a bucket. Once you have 15 buckets of dragon manure, use them to fill a compost bin and then close it. Ultracompost takes 90 minutes to decompose in a bin, and each bin needs 15 buckets of dragon manure to produce ultracompost.",
"Marrentill seed",
"Utilising either bladed dive or dive with mobile will greatly speed up the processing rate. When finished opening the chest with all keys from your inventory and pack yak, teleport to War's Retreat to restock on keys. After loading a preset that replenishes the keys in your inventory, surge north and enter the boss portal to The Zamorakian Undercity. Next surge south then north-west to the building with the chest. Profits can be further increased by using the cave nightshade and poison ivy berries to craft weapon poison++.",
"The closed chest, located in the Yanille Agility dungeon, always rewards nine herbs when opened: three grimy ranarr, two grimy harralander, and one each of grimy torstol, grimy irit, grimy avantoe and grimy kwuarm. Opening the chest requires a sinister key, and the key is used up when the chest is opened. Depending on the price difference between the keys and the herbs, it can be very profitable to buy sinister keys, open the chest, and sell the resulting herbs.",
"Make your way to the Lava Maze with 28 muddy keys in your inventory either by running, using teleports, or using the canoe. Slash the webs apart and avoid the hellhounds (or turn on Protect from Melee), and make your way to the muddy chest at the end. Run to the nearest cape seller/banker to the west of the Lava Maze and refill your inventory with keys using a preset. Sometimes a roaming banker will be within sight when you leave the maze so use this bank when possible.",
"Obelisk shard or Portable obelisk",
"Hard Wilderness achievements completed to choose the destination of obelisk teleports",
"Fremennik equipment patch",
"Wilderness hilt",
"Ancient warriors' equipment patch",
