"Necromancy cape (recommended)",
"Wear an Alteration necklace.",
"60 (103 recommended for multiply III glyphs)",
"Underworld Grimoire 4 recommended for +15% necroplasm",
"Necromancy cape recommended unlimited alteration glyph perk",
"Alteration necklace recommended if using alteration glyphs",
"Performing lesser necroplasm rituals",
"Money making guide/Performing lesser necroplasm rituals",
"Weak necroplasm",
"Responding to ritual disturbances will improve return on investment and experience rates, but reduce the number of rituals per hour and outputs.",
"Placing the weak necroplasm in the focus storage will save more time than replacing the focus prior to each ritual. Ensuring the durability of the light sources and glyphs are consistent will result in fewer repairs.",
"A cheaper way to gather buckets of slime (without Magic notepaper) is to use Morytania legs 2, Morytania legs 3, or Morytania legs 4 which grant 5, 10, or unlimited free daily teleports to the Ectofuntus slime pool, respectively.",
"Put War's Retreat Teleport on your main skilling/non-combat action bar and have that as your primary bar. Right click on your (equipped) explorer's ring 3, cabbage-port, then start plucking in organised fashion so you can always walk two steps over to the next cabbage. Going across rows each time is advised. Once your inventory is full, teleport to War's Retreat and go to the bank chest. Hit 3 to bank-all and Esc to exit with your cursor already on your explorer's ring. Repeat.",
"As an alternative for free players without the War's Retreat Teleport, the Skull of Remembrance from the quest The Death of Chivalry can be used to teleport close to a bank chest.",
"After 5 worlds, you should have 28 berries. Banking is fastest with War's Retreat Teleport, then use Archaeology journal to teleport back. If you have not unlocked War's Retreat Teleport, you can bank with the journal. 25 runs are possible in 1 hour.",
"68 Farming",
"240 Coins are needed only for the charter ship; the Karamja lodestone is no cost. Juju teleport spiritbag cost can be eliminated using the witchdoctor mask. Coconuts grow on palm trees, and they're used to make coconut milk, used in high-level Herblore. They're also used to pay farmers to look after magic trees. Once a palm tree has grown fully, it can be harvested repeatedly, with a coconut growing back every 45 minutes for a maximum of six. Harvest the coconuts and note them with the tool leprechaun at any patch if inventory becomes full.",
"Can be done every 270 minutes; a run takes about 4 minutes.",
"Teleport to Castle Wars using a ring of duelling, use Fairy ring code CIQ, or the Yanille lodestone for the fruit tree patch near Tree Gnome Village, west of the maze.",
"Use Charter a ship to Brimhaven, use a brimhaven tablet, or take the Karamja lodestone to get to the patch, south of the docks.",
"Potatoes can be found in potato fields, and the best free-to-play location is north of the Lumbridge cow pen. Starting off at the Varrock lodestone, walk the road south, going through the fence. The potato field is directly to the south east. Use of Surge can reduce travel time.",
"Teleport to the Burthorpe lodestone and bank there. Teleport back to the Varrock lodestone and run back to the potato field to continue picking potatoes.",
"The archaeology professor is located inside the Exam Centre.",
"The archaeology professor is located at the Depths excavation site, requiring completion of the research On the Threshold of the Mind. This requires 103 Archaeology and 95 Dungeoneering, as well as a restored 'friendship bracelet', which can be added to the toolbelt.",
"The archaeology professor is located near the Stadio debris in the far southeast portion of the dig site.",
"The archaeology professor is located in the southwest portion of the Vestibule of Futility, requiring completion of the Embrace the Chaos mystery (requiring 29 Archaeology) to access.",
"The Archeology professor is located behind the crumbled wall next to the Orcus altar. No Agility level is required to traverse it, but players must have a restored Pontifex signet ring (requiring 58 Archaeology) with them or on their toolbelt to access the chapel.",
"The archaeology professor is located at the Moksha ritual site excavation site. Completion of the Know Thy Measure mystery is required to access the site, and the Associate qualification is required to access Orthen at all.",
"Senntisten Dig Site",
"The archaeology professor is located near the bridge leading to Thalmund's Forge. Completion of the Out of the Crucible mystery (requiring 83 Archaeology) is required to access the area.",
"Use a mystical sand seed or regular sand seed to quickly teleport to the Garden of Kharid. Otherwise you can use a ring of duelling or the Al Kharid lodestone and run north. Once here, pickpocket either of the Crux Eqal Knights near the edges.",
"Use the Grouping System to quickly teleport to the Liberation of Mazcab. Otherwise one may use the World window, which is northwest of Menaphos. Once here, run west to pickpocket any of the Goebie scavengers.",
"Use the Menaphos lodestone then run north to the Menaphos Merchant district. Leela's favour or a Merchant district teleport tablet can get you there directly.",
"Use a TokKul-Zo to quickly teleport to the Main Plaza of TzHaar City. If not owned, use the Karamja lodestone and run through Brimhaven to the volcano entrance. Once here, pickpocket either of the TzHaar-Hur traders near the northern corners of the main plaza.",
"Shiny columbarium key",
"Use Drakan's medallion to quickly teleport to Darkmeyer. Pickpocket the Vyrewatch tither in the building north of the thievable chests (marked on the minimap). The ring of Vitur is especially useful as it prevents aggression from vyres. Without it, players should ensure that the room is cleared of vyrelords/vyreladies and the door remains closed.",
"Vyrewatch might enter the room and be aggressive",
"Use stardust from the currency pouch or the Wicked hood to quickly teleport to Wizards Tower.",
"Fairy traders can be found in Zanaris market. A cut diamond is required per entry unless A Fairy Tale III - Battle at Ork's Rift is completed, in which case entry is free.",
"Being in Ardougne, players only need to complete the medium Ardougne achievements to obtain the +10% success chance buff, instead of the hard Ardougne achievements, significantly reducing the barrier to entry. They can be found in Ardougne castle and Ardougne market. Pickpocketing them in the castle is recommended as they are easier to trap in a corner, preventing movement. Pickpocketing in Ardougne market has an advantage in that it is nearer a bank, but players should have ample inventory space to bring food without needing to get more from the bank.",
"Ardougne market",
"Use Drakan's medallion to quickly teleport to Darkmeyer. The ring of Vitur is recommended for getting into position as it prevents aggression from vyres, but players should switch to a luck ring after (if not using a luck relic) as Tier 2 or higher luck (improves up to Tier 4) boosts the chance of receiving the ring of Vitur as a drop. Players have two options here.",
"Double Escape codex",
"Screening ancient gravel",
"Money making guide/Screening ancient gravel",
"The Archaeology soil box should be used to increase amount of gravel screened per hour. It also makes the process less click-intensive.",
"Non-members will not be able to use the waterfiend familiar and will have to run to deposit materials at the nearby material bank every inventory. Crucially they can only get low amounts of materials due to being capped to level 20, making it much less profitable.",
"1 Crafting",
"Start by teleporting to Burthorpe. Walk south until you hit the sheep pen (across from the cows near Burthorpe mine. Shear the sheep until your inventory is full. Walk straight to the spinning wheel (north of the cow pen) and turn it into balls of wool. Walk north to the bank chest and deposit it. The whole process takes about 2:29. Rinse and repeat for as long as you like. Once you're ready, teleport to the Exchange and sell them.",
"Wool",
"Smelting adamant bars",
