"Plain smithing urn or Strong smithing urn recommended for better experience rates.",
"Artisan workshop",
"Smelting iron bars",
"Money making guide/Smelting iron bars",
"10 Smithing",
"19 Smithing (recommended)",
"It is recommended that the player has at least level 19 to do this method, since at that level you have a 10% chance of doubling a bar without using any resources while smelting. It should take around 52 seconds to make an inventory full of iron bars, deposit them into your metal bank and then start the process over again.",
"Mithril bar",
"Necronium bar",
"Orikalkum bar",
"Smelting rune bars",
"Money making guide/Smelting rune bars",
"57 Smithing (recommended)",
"It's recommended that the player is at least level 57 to do this method since at that level you have a 10% chance of doubling a bar without using any resources while smelting, as well as reducing the smelting speed from 3 seconds to 1.8 seconds. It should take around 52 seconds to make an inventory of rune bars, deposit them into your metal bank and then start the process over again.",
"Perfect juju smithing potion (4)",
"TOURIST_TRAP",
"The Tourist Trap",
"members",
"Use any anvil to forge adamant bars into dart tips. Noted adamant bars can be added to the metal bank and then withdrawn, as adamant dart tips are stackable there is no need to bank. You can queue up smithing multiple sets of adamant dart tips by right clicking the anvil, choosing \"open smithing interface\" and selecting adamant dart tips until you have a full inventory of unfinished smithing items. You will then start to smith the dart tips, automatically starting to smith the next unfinished item as each is completed. Maintain high heat by using a forge to progress in creating nails at the fastest rate.",
"Smithing cannonballs",
"Money making guide/Smithing cannonballs",
"35 Smithing",
"Morytania legs 2 or better (Medium Morytania achievements)",
"DWARF_CANNON",
"Dwarf Cannon",
"Ghosts Ahoy (recommended)",
"Morytania legs 2 are rewarded for completing all the medium Morytania achievements. When they are worn, cannonballs are smithed twice as fast at the furnace in Port Phasmatys. Steel bars may be stored in and used directly from the metal bank.",
"Port Phasmatys furnace; Morytania legs 2 apply the speed bonus here",
"Use any anvil to forge elder rune bars into shields. Noted elder rune bars can be added to the metal bank and then withdrawn. You can queue up smithing multiple shields by right clicking the anvil, choosing \"open smithing interface\" and selecting elder rune shields until you have a full inventory of unfinished smithing items. You will then start to smith the shields, automatically starting to smith the next unfinished item as each is completed. Maintain high heat by using a forge to progress in creating shields at the fastest rate.",
"Glorious bars are used in the creation of masterwork equipment. This method involves creating glorious bars from scratch, which can be done at any anvil except the anvil in Ashdale.",
"Use any anvil to forge rune bars into arrowheads. Noted rune bars can be added to the metal bank and then withdrawn, as rune arrowheads are stackable there is no need to bank. You can queue up smithing multiple sets of rune arrowheads by right clicking the anvil, choosing \"open smithing interface\" and selecting rune arrowheads until you have a full inventory of unfinished smithing items. You will then start to smith the arrowheads, automatically starting to smith the next unfinished item as each is completed. Maintain high heat by using a forge to progress in creating arrowheads at the fastest rate.",
"Use any anvil to forge rune bars into rune bolts (unf). Noted rune bars can be added to the metal bank and then withdrawn, as rune bolts (unf) are stackable there is no need to bank. You can queue up smithing multiple sets of rune bolts (unf) by right clicking the anvil, choosing \"open smithing interface\" and selecting rune bolts (unf) until you have a full inventory of unfinished smithing items. You will then start to smith the bolts, automatically starting to smith the next unfinished item as each is completed. Maintain high heat by using a forge to progress in creating bolts at the fastest rate.",
"Use any anvil to forge rune bars into dart tips. Noted rune bars can be added to the metal bank and then withdrawn, as rune dart tips are stackable there is no need to bank. You can queue up smithing multiple sets of rune dart tips by right clicking the anvil, choosing \"open smithing interface\" and selecting rune dart tips until you have a full inventory of unfinished smithing items. You will then start to smith the dart tips, automatically starting to smith the next unfinished item as each is completed. Maintain high heat by using a forge to progress in creating nails at the fastest rate.",
"Use any anvil to forge rune bars into nails. Noted rune bars can be added to the metal bank and then withdrawn, as rune knives are stackable there is no need to bank. You can queue up smithing multiple rune knives by right clicking the anvil, choosing \"open smithing interface\" and selecting rune knives until you have a full inventory of unfinished smithing items. You will then start to smith the knives, automatically starting to smith the next unfinished item as each is completed. Maintain high heat by using a forge to progress in creating knives at the fastest rate.",
"Any anvil, e.g. at Artisans' Workshop",
"Use any anvil to forge steel bars into nails. Noted steel bars can be added to the metal bank and then withdrawn, as steel nails are stackable there is no need to bank. You can queue up smithing multiple sets of steel nails by right clicking the anvil, choosing \"open smithing interface\" and selecting steel nails until you have a full inventory of unfinished smithing items. You will then start to smith the nails, automatically starting to smith the next unfinished item as each is completed. Maintain high heat by using a forge to progress in creating nails at the fastest rate.",
"Spinning flax",
"Money making guide/Spinning flax",
"The wire machine can be found in the south-west area of the city, east of a furnace. The wire respawns in 6 seconds after being taken. One trip of 28 wires takes about 5 minutes. It is possible to achieve higher profits (and additional Magic experience) by casting High Level Alchemy on a noted stack of any profitable item while waiting for the wire to spawn. Several casts can be fit into the 6-second respawn period without affecting the rate of wires stolen. Alternatively disassembling items can also be done whilst waiting.",
"Vegetable Stalls can be found at the market in Lumbridge. Repeatedly steal from the stall until your inventory is full, and then bank all of your items at the nearby bank chest. It takes slightly over 1 minute to get a full inventory; about 50 runs can be completed per hour.",
"It takes around 18 seconds to turn an inventory of 14 unstrung magic longbows and 14 bowstrings into 14 magic longbows. Bank presets are highly recommended for this method. Players can also put the unstrung bow on their action bar and assign a key bind, which can be the same button as the one for their preset. This can make the process even easier. Using a portable fletcher can be useful for this method. It grants a 10% experience boost, as well as a 10% chance to string two bows at once, potentially speeding up the process.",
"It takes around 18 seconds to turn an inventory of 14 unstrung magic shortbows and 14 bowstrings into 14 magic shortbows; maintaining this rate for an hour would result in 2,800 bows strung. Bank presets are highly recommended for this method, allowing the use of a bank's \"Load Last Preset\" option for more efficiency. Players can also put the unstrung bow on their action bar and assign a key bind, which can be the same button as the one for their preset. This can make the process even easier. Using a portable fletcher can be useful for this method. It grants a 10% experience boost, as well as a 10% chance to string two bows at once, potentially speeding up the process.",
"It takes around 18 seconds to turn an inventory of 14 unstrung maple shortbows and 14 bowstrings into 14 maple shortbows. Bank presets are highly recommended for this method. Players can also put the unstrung bow on their action bar and assign a key bind, which can be the same button as the one for their preset. This can make the process even easier. Using a portable fletcher can be useful for this method. It grants a 10% experience boost, as well as a 10% chance to string two bows at once, potentially speeding up the process.",
"It takes around 18 seconds to turn an inventory of 14 unstrung oak longbows and 14 bowstrings into 14 oak longbows. Bank presets are highly recommended for this method. Players can also put the unstrung bow on their action bar and assign a key bind, which can be the same button as the one for their preset. This can make the process even easier. Using a portable fletcher can be useful for this method. It grants a 10% experience boost, as well as a 10% chance to string two bows at once, potentially speeding up the process.",
"It takes around 18 seconds to turn an inventory of 14 unstrung willow longbows and 14 bowstrings into 14 willow longbows. Bank presets are highly recommended for this method. Players can also put the unstrung bow on their action bar and assign a key bind, which can be the same button as the one for their preset. This can make the process even easier. Using a portable fletcher can be useful for this method. It grants a 10% experience boost, as well as a 10% chance to string two bows at once, potentially speeding up the process.",
"It takes around 18 seconds to turn an inventory of 14 unstrung yew longbows and 14 bowstrings into 14 yew longbows. Bank presets are highly recommended for this method. Players can also put the unstrung bow on their action bar and assign a key bind, which can be the same button as the one for their preset. This can make the process even easier. Using a portable fletcher can be useful for this method. It grants a 10% experience boost, as well as a 10% chance to string two bows at once, potentially speeding up the process.",
"A portable well can be placed next to a bank, and has a right click option to take vials of water. You then need to type the number of vials to be taken. The exact number does not need to be typed and as such typing 111 or 33 may be faster than typing 28 exactly, as any excess over the number of available inventory spaces will simply be ignored.",
"2 Crafting",
"Royal dragon leather is used to train Crafting, and it is always in high demand. Because Royal dragonhide must be tanned into leather before it can be crafted, tanning the hides in bulk can be highly profitable.",
"Smelting steel bars",
