"Bought from the shops at 550 GP each: the item's value, which the Wiki guide uses as the shop price.",
"Bought from the shops at 410 GP each: the item's value, which the Wiki guide uses as the shop price.",
"Can be done every 1 week; a run takes about 10 minutes.",
"Many types of runes can be bought from various rune shops for considerably less than their Grand Exchange market value. Many of these shops hold a stock of 7,000 of the basic elemental runes, of which most notably water runes, fire runes, and soul runes yield a notable profit when sold in the Grand Exchange. Upon arriving at a shop, purchase all of the profitable runes (see Outputs above).",
"Shops restock runes over 1 week so runs can be done more than just once a week, but will have a reduced number available.",
"Make sure you are opted out of PvP or return to Edgeville and bank all your items. Head south to the ruined building in Edgeville and travel to level 51 Wilderness by pulling the Edgeville teleport lever. Exit the Deserted Keep you find yourself in by cutting through the cobweb blocking the way north, and head west to a small ruined building north of the Mage Arena. Cut through the two cobwebs blocking the way and pull the lever to be transported to the small cave where Lundail runs his Arena-side Rune Shop. This is a safe area that is not considered part of the Wilderness and also contains a bank.",
"Various rune shops around RuneScape",
"Make sure you are opted out of PvP or return to Edgeville and bank all your items. Head south to the ruined building in Edgeville and travel to level 51 Wilderness by pulling the Edgeville teleport lever. Exit the Deserted Keep you find yourself in by cutting through the cobweb blocking the way north, and head west to a small ruined building north of the Mage Arena. Cut through the two cobwebs blocking the way and pull the lever to be transported to the small cave where Lundail runs his Arena-side Rune Shop. This is a safe area that is not considered part of the Wilderness and also contains a bank. Players who own the Slayer cape may get here faster by using it to teleport to Mandrith and then running east.",
