"Olive oil (3)",
"Can be done every 24 hours; a run takes about 50 minutes.",
"Razmire General Store and Razmire Builders' Merchants are two shops run by Razmire Keelgan in Mort'ton. Buying some of the items he sells (olive oil, limestone bricks, planks and possibly limestone) and banking them in Burgh de Rott can be profitable. Limestone often has a better profit margin than limestone bricks, but they are usually harder to re-sell. It's of course not necessary to buy all of the items listed here -- perhaps you just want to buy the olive oil and the planks, depending on the current prices.",
"Mort'ton, Burgh de Rott",
"The games necklace can be used to teleport to Burgh de Rott with the completion of The Darkness of Hallowvale quest and having 500 companion levels in Temple Trekking.",
"A Swamp Boat can be taken nearby to Mort'ton from the Hollows in the Mort Myre Swamp.",
"Run south from Canifis (with a shortcut via the tunnel behind the Hair of the Dog tavern after In Search of the Myreque).",
"buying-supplies-from-the-stonemason.standard",
"Buying supplies from the Stonemason",
"Money making guide/Buying supplies from the Stonemason",
"Bought from the shops at 21 GP each: the item's value, which the Wiki guide uses as the shop price.",
"Bought from the shops at 325,000 GP each: the item's value, which the Wiki guide uses as the shop price.",
"Bought from the shops at 130,000 GP each: the item's value, which the Wiki guide uses as the shop price.",
"Bought from the shops at 975,000 GP each: the item's value, which the Wiki guide uses as the shop price.",
"The Keldagrim Stonemason shop run by the Stonemason in Keldagrim supplies a small number of expensive construction materials. One of these, gold leaves is consistently profitable to buy from him and sell on the Grand Exchange. Purchase the items listed in the Outputs section above with non-zero quantities; those listed at zero quantity are either not profitable or do not have a high enough trade volume to support reliable sales.",
"First time from the Keldagrim entrance tunnel east of Rellekka.",
"The Luck of the Dwarves or Hazelmere's signet ring provide unlimited teleports to the west side of the Palace ground floor.",
"Players with access to Keldagrim can use the Keldagrim trapdoor in the north-west of the Grand Exchange to arrive in East Keldagrim. A luck ring such as the Ring of Wealth or higher variants can also teleport a short distance from the trapdoor using the Grand Exchange teleport option.",
"The master camouflage outfit provides unlimited teleports to the Consortium (0, 1), the top floor of the palace in the centre of Keldagrim. This allows convenient access to both the east and west side of Keldagrim. Other variants of this outfit will also teleport players to this location five times per day.",
"buying-vials-of-water.standard",
"Buying vials of water",
"Money making guide/Buying vials of water",
"HORROR_FROM_THE_DEEP",
"Horror from the Deep",
"Ancient Awakening",
"Karamja gloves 3 recommended for teleportation",
"Granny Rowan's Supplies shop requires tier 2 of the Botanist's Workbench",
"Bought from the shops at 10 GP each: the item's value, which the Wiki guide uses as the shop price.",
"Bought from the shops at 5 GP each: the item's value, which the Wiki guide uses as the shop price.",
"Can be done every 1 week; a run takes about 4 minutes.",
"Vials of water are used in Herblore, and are always in demand on the Grand Exchange. They are much cheaper in the shops than on the Grand Exchange, so a profit can be made easily by buying vial of water from the shops and selling on the Grand Exchange. With the addition of bomb vials that can be bought from Jatix in Taverley, Lady Meilyr in Prifddinas and Granny Rowan in Fort Forinthry one can significantly increase profit at little to no time cost.",
"1. Teleport to the Taverley lodestone and head south-east to Jatix.",
"3. Use the Lighthouse Teleport (must have completed Horror from the Deep) and head upstairs to Jossik.",
"4. Use the Juju teleport spiritbag (must have completed Shilo Village) and head west into Shilo Village to Obli (general store). For a faster route, if you have Karamja gloves 3, use its teleport and walk south from the gem mine.",
"Lady Meilyr, Jatix, Jossik, Obli, Granny Rowan",
"Use 1. Teleport to the Taverley lodestone and head south-east to Jatix.",
