"Woodcutting: Hatchet of bloom and blight recommended",
"Scripture of Bik (recommended)",
"Pontifex shadow ring (recommended)",
"Extreme magic (3)",
"Extreme ranging (3)",
"Super restore (3)",
"Stinkshroom spore",
"Fragments of Pernix's quiver",
"Assumes the guide's 10 actions per hour. Adjust it to your own pace.",
"Your actual profit may be higher or lower depending on your upgrades.",
"It's highly recommended to fully upgrade and overcharge the Pontifex shadow ring, it's possible to obtain 10 Elder Trove (Bik, T3) an hour which will give the best money making possible.",
"To obtain an Elder trove, xp has to be gained within the range of 6:00 to 12:00 minutes whilst being in the Croesus Front; The time delay will depend on the tier of the player's Pontifex shadow ring. It's possible to leave the Croesus front and return to trigger another Elder trove drop, this is useful if you are training another skill that isn't possible within the Croesus front.",
"High tier augmented tools do not affect your troves per hour and only increase your assumed xp per hour. If you are training a different skill and using the above method to accumulate Troves, the tools on your Tool Belt are adequate.",
"It's highly recommended to use the Grace of the Elves to gain Seren spirits and make use of porters. Alternatively Magic notepaper can be used to save on porters, but this will be less afk. Use of the porters isn't required if Fishing and you're using the Fury shark outfit's destroy function.",
"collecting-anti-dragon-shields.standard",
"Collecting anti-dragon shields",
"Money making guide/Collecting anti-dragon shields",
"DRAGON_SLAYER",
"Dragon Slayer",
"40 recommended for Dragon Slayer",
"37 recommended for Dragon Slayer",
"After completing the quest Dragon Slayer, you may return to Duke Horacio on the floor 1 above ground of Lumbridge Castle at any time to obtain more Anti-dragon shields. The Duke will give you a new shield even if you already have one in your inventory, so the drop trick is not necessary for this method. Speak to the Duke and press the space bar to advance his dialogue, then press the \"1\" key to select the dialogue option \"I seek a shield that will protect me from dragonbreath.\" Hold the space bar to advance the Duke's dialogue until he gives you a shield, then rinse and repeat. Alternatively, if you unlock your GUI, you can drag the NPC dialogue box so that it overlaps with the Duke. Doing this, you can simply hold down the space bar and click both the Duke and the shield dialogue option without needing to move your mouse.",
"With high efficiency, you can obtain one shield in about four seconds. You can convert a full inventory of 27 (26 if you already have noted shields in your inventory) Anti-dragon shields into notes at the same time by using a shield on a piece of Magic notepaper. Take care not to left click on the shield, as this will equip it rather than using it.",
"floor 1 above ground of Lumbridge Castle",
"collecting-blue-dragon-scales.standard",
"Collecting blue dragon scales",
"Money making guide/Collecting blue dragon scales",
"Dusty key (if not 70)",
"Blue dragon scale",
"Assumes the guide's 900 actions per hour. Adjust it to your own pace.",
"The better place to collect them is the resource dungeon as they're closer together and there are more of them, but that area requires 60 Dungeoneering to access. Without the resource dungeon, you can collect about 550 scales per hour, compared to 900 inside the resource dungeon. 70 Agility is also recommended to avoid having to traverse Taverley Dungeon, which would require a dusty key. A Beast of Burden like the spirit terrorbird, war tortoise, or pack yak are also very helpful to cut down on banking time.",
"The Obelisk of Water on an island can only be reached by traversing the dungeon. The island is just off the coast near Catherby. There is a one-way mithril grapple shortcut from the island to the shore which requires 36 Agility, 39 Ranged, and 22 Strength.",
"collecting-dinosaur-propellant.standard",
"Collecting dinosaur 'propellant'",
"Money making guide/Collecting dinosaur 'propellant'",
"95 Firemaking",
"The rate assume 625 actions are performed per hour, approximately 23 inventories or 2:35 per cycle. It takes a significant amount of time to travel between stations and feed all the Rex babies and then 3 ticks (1.8 seconds) to burn each Potterington Blend #102 Fertiliser. For optimal rates it is suggested you use mobile, double surge, and bladed dive. It is recommended you travel in a circle to each trough and completely feed each Rex baby before moving to the next trough. After feeding each Rex baby once from each trough convert your inventory and repeat the cycle.",
"One of the possible rotations is starting at the barn.",
"Beanasaurus Rex (beany mush trough).",
"Berrisaurus Rex (berry mush trough).",
"Branasaurus Rex (cerealy mush trough).",
"Eggsperimentation",
"collecting-dinosaur-eggs-from-seggregation.standard",
"Collecting dinosaur eggs from seggregation",
"Money making guide/Collecting dinosaur eggs from seggregation",
"Dinosaur eggs can be collected quickly from the Seggregation activity by collecting eggs from the pile of dinosaur eggs and destroying the good and bad eggs. This allows the dinosaur eggs which are occasionally found during this activity to be obtained rapidly as there is no need to move between stations in order to produce sharp shell shards.",
"collecting-grapes.standard",
"Collecting grapes",
"Money making guide/Collecting grapes",
"32 Cooking",
"Chef's hat",
"Grapes spawn on the top floor of the Cooks' Guild. Due to the long respawn time, this method requires world switching to gather grapes more quickly.",
"Each trip takes 7.5 minutes, or 8 trips per hour. This may vary significantly based on how fast world switching can be done.",
"While there is also a spawn for grapes in the Phoenix Gang Hideout, it is further from a bank.",
"If you do not want to switch worlds, you can use another method in conjunction, such as Fletching headless arrows, because Fletching doesn't require banking or a lot of inventory spaces. Profit varies depending on the combinations of methods.",
"The Cooks' Guild is just west of Varrock; a skills necklace can teleport to its entrance. Entry requires 32 Cooking and a chef's hat or sous chef's toque; members can use a Cooking cape or max cape instead. Completing hard Varrock achievements also removes the headgear requirement.",
"collecting-harmonic-dust.standard",
"Collecting harmonic dust",
"Money making guide/Collecting harmonic dust",
"Harmonic dust can be obtained by playing harps within the Ithell district of Prifddinas. Harps are a very low effort way of training crafting, and the harmonic dust has many uses. Once you have acquired all of the crystal items you need, the dust can be made into items and sold for profit - this is a nice supplementary income whilst training crafting. If you're planning on staying at harps for many hours, it's worth buying crystal armour seeds or crystal weapon seeds earlier than you need as they can take awhile to buy on the GE. Approximately 750 dust can be obtained an hour without VoS (or artificer's measure) at level 99 Crafting.",
"Ithell district of Prifddinas",
"collecting-honeycomb.standard",
"Collecting honeycomb",
"Money making guide/Collecting honeycomb",
"Insect repellent",
"Honeycomb",
"Honeycombs are used to make honey badger pouches. They can be extracted from the beehives East of Manor Farm behind the large pen. This requires insect repellent, which can be stored in the toolbelt. Extracting honeycomb is a click-intensive process as you have to right-click and select \"Honey\" for each one you want, though you can skip the animation of the character collecting the honeycomb by re-clicking the honey option on the same beehive.",
"collecting-jangerberries.standard",
"Collecting jangerberries",
"Money making guide/Collecting jangerberries",
"10 Agility",
"Member",
"Starting at the Castle Wars lobby with only a rope in your inventory and a ring of duelling equipped, run straight east to the island. Use Surge to either cross the bridge or after the point where the character last turns before the lake to speed up the trip. Then, use the rope on the tree branch, jumping over to the island (this will use up the rope).",
"Ogre island south-west of Yanille / lodestone",
"Use Home Teleport to Yanille lodestone.",
"Use Watchtower Teleport, toggled to Yanille after completing the Ardougne Set Tasks - Hard.",
"Use Ring of duelling teleport to Castle Wars.",
"To the north lies the Fight Arena, the Tree Gnome Village, a Monastery, Port Khazard and (further north) East Ardougne.",
"The Yanille lodestone is the closest to the fairy ring network.",
"The Edgeville lodestone, however, is the closest to both a bank and a fairy ring.",
"The Al Kharid lodestone is closest to the gnome glider network.",
"The Port Sarim lodestone is closest to a charter ship port.",
"collecting-limpwurt-roots.standard",
"Collecting limpwurt roots",
"Money making guide/Collecting limpwurt roots",
"20 Dungeoneering",
"Brass key",
"53 Combat (recommended)",
"As they are level 26, Hill Giants are aggressive to any player with a combat level of 52 or less, which may be an annoyance to the gathering process. It is therefore recommended to have at least level 53 combat.",
"Edgeville Dungeon hill giant resource dungeon",
"collecting-memory-shards.standard",
"Collecting memory shards",
"Money making guide/Collecting memory shards",
"Portent of restoration VII",
"Memory shards may be obtained from pickpocketing, checking hunter traps, or planting seeds, when the relevant passive perk (for each method) is active from the Memorial to Guthix. When memory shards are earned, it will prompt the message \"You find a small fragment of a memory\".",
"Memory shards can also be obtained in the Hall of Memories while harvesting memories when the buff from getting close to a recollection butterfly is active.",
"Each time you obtain memory shards the amount varies, so it's possible to get as low as 400 and as high as 800 per hour depending on luck. For this guide 600 memory shards has been used as an average obtained per hour.",
"Memory shards can be converted into porters, with the best conversation rate being Sign of the porter IV with 1.25 charges per shard.",
"Profit per hour column is based on converting 600 memory shards.",
"collecting-mort-myre-fungi.standard",
"Collecting mort myre fungi",
"Money making guide/Collecting mort myre fungi",
"40 Thieving",
"36 Woodcutting",
"Silver sickle (b) or equivalent",
"NATURE_SPIRIT",
"Nature Spirit",
"A Fairy Tale II - Cure a Queen (partially, only enough to use fairy rings)",
"81 Farming (recommended)",
"Morytania legs 1 or higher (highly recommended)",
"TokKul-Zo recommended for banking (requires completion of The Elder Kiln) in combination with a dramen or lunar staff (unless A Fairy Tale III - Battle at Ork's Rift has been completed)",
"Deadliest Catch recommended to unlock a deposit chest to speed up emptying the inventory (optional, but will save you a lot of time, because you'll need to bank only once an hour to restock on prayer renewals).",
"Ouroboros pouch optional to eliminate the damage from ghasts",
"Armour if player has low defence.",
"Uncapped Potential Perk from Player Owned Farms",
"Collecting mort myre fungi is very profitable as it is the secondary ingredient for making super energy potions. While wearing Morytania legs, players will receive double the amount of fungi when collecting. However, make sure there are at least two inventory spaces when collecting, otherwise players will only receive one fungus. Casting bloom affects rotting objects in the 8 squares around the player and consumes between 10 and 60 prayer points (though if the player only has 1 prayer point left, bloom can still be cast). Players should use a location surrounded by 3 rotting logs to increase the chances of obtaining mort myre fungus. An Ivandis flail or blessed silver sickle can be placed on the action bar to cast bloom with hotkeys. Players should use the three logs south of the Deposit Box as those are the most efficient. Gathering the fungus by prioritising the logs in the order of South-west, west, then East, you can cast bloom as soon as the mushrooms on the east log disappears, even though your character doesn't appear to be in the center yet. If the fungus on the logs disappears, it indicates that your character has reached that point even if it isn't shown. Using this, you will increase your fungus output by a decent amount.",
"Fairy ring BKR is located within the swamp.",
"Fairy ring ALQ is located in the Haunted Woods. Run southwest to enter the swamp area.",
"Fairy ring CKS is located just north of Mort Myre. Run south through the gate to enter the swamp.",
"Upon reaching a combined total level of 100 in Temple Trekking, the gate at the north end of Mort Myre may also be used to quick-travel to the Nature Grotto near the south end of the swamp.",
"For people that haven't completed Deadliest Catch: first, use the fairy ring network to teleport to BKR. Run west until you see three rotting logs, as shown in the image above. Drink a dose of prayer renewal, stand in the middle of the 3 rotting logs and cast bloom. Mort myre fungi will not spawn every time. Always pick the northern log last because when picked, you will return to the middle, removing the need to click back. After a full inventory, teleport to the TzHaar Fight Cave with the TokKul-Zo to bank and repeat using the fairy ring just north. Alternatively, if you haven't got a TokKul-Zo, use the fairy ring to bank in Zanaris, although this is slightly slower.",
"Alternatively, players who complete the easy Ardougne achievements (Requires: Biohazard, Gertrude's Cat, Monk's Friend, Plague City, Tower of Life; 15 Fishing, 16 Thieving, 10 Construction), can use the Kandarin monastery Teleport after collecting fungi (but before banking with the TokKul-Zo ) to recharge their prayer point for free. The Kandarin monastery Teleport is a one click teleport spell that isn't interrupted by attacking ghasts unlike the TokKul-Zo. Return with a fairy ring as mentioned above.",
"collecting-sharp-shell-shards.standard",
"Collecting sharp shell shards",
"Money making guide/Collecting sharp shell shards",
"Sharp shell shard",
"Obtained numbers will not be exact but very approximate, as converting eggs gives randomly between 12 to 15 shards each.",
"Dive/Bladed Dive and Surge are very useful to travel between the pile, compost bin and incubator deposits, which may increase hourly yield, but also increasing intensity.",
"Using the Shadow-Touched set may also increase XP gained, but in this method, it is possible to use Grace of the elves, as collecting the eggs gives 1 Farming experience, triggering the appearance of the Seren spirit.",
"Thanks to the quickly ticking Farming exp, this method may also be useful to collect Master farmer fragments.",
"The usage of a Beast of Burden is also possible, reducing necessary trips to the egg pile, but since the distance between deposits is small, its impact is relatively small.",
"collecting-swamp-tar-from-the-lady-zay.standard",
"Collecting swamp tar from the Lady Zay",
"Money making guide/Collecting swamp tar from the Lady Zay",
"Lunar Diplomacy started",
"The Lady Zay has many barrels of swamp tar on its decks, which can be looted for substantial profit. Start out by using the Lunar Isle lodestone, and run to the docks and board the Lady Zay. Go down the stairs in the southern end of the ship, and you'll see four barrels of swamp tar. Go to one of them and start clicking on it until it's empty. Do the same for the other three barrels -- the amount of tar varies between 1 and at least 15, but it'll average about three per barrel. Head back to the first barrel you looted, waiting for the tar to spawn again, and start the cycle over again. It takes about 22 seconds for the tar to respawn and is not dependent on the population of the world.",
"The tar of course stacks, so you'll never have to bank. When you're finished, go to the Grand Exchange and sell the swamp tar, which shouldn't be too difficult as it's a high-volume item.",
"Lady Zay",
"Start out by using the Lunar Isle lodestone, and run to the docks and board the Lady Zay. Go down the stairs in the southern end of the ship, and you'll see four barrels of swamp tar. Go to one of them and start clicking on it until it's empty. Do the same for the other three barrels -- the amount of tar varies between 1 and at least 15, but it'll average about three per barrel. Head back to the first barrel you looted, waiting for the tar to spawn again, and start the cycle over again. It takes about 22 seconds for the tar to respawn and is not dependent on the population of the world.",
"collecting-swamp-toads.standard",
"Collecting swamp toads",
"Money making guide/Collecting swamp toads",
"The legs can be quickly pulled off on the run from the swamp to the bank. This usually lowers the value, so be sure to check the prices of both.",
"collecting-tempered-fungal-shafts.standard",
"Collecting tempered fungal shafts",
"Money making guide/Collecting tempered fungal shafts",
"82 Fletching",
"82 Firemaking",
"82 Fletching or 82 Firemaking",
"Crystal knife recommended (if fletching)",
"Zanarian zygomite (unchecked)",
"Daemoncap zygomite (unchecked)",
"Arcspore zygomite (unchecked)",
"Non-stop cutting would result in 1,200 actions per hour as shafts take five ticks to make.",
"Its highly recommened to only cut the Scruffy zygomites while using crystal knife since it gives a 5% chance to double shafts while fletching and does not degrade when carestyling.",
"The best Scruffy zygomite to cut is the one closest to the waiting line due to having the shortest animation.",
"Drying the Scruffy zygomites for experience in Firemaking is not considered as the crystal knife can't be used to boost the output but if you don't have a Crystal knife feel free to do this.",
"Zygomite Carestyling",
"collecting-white-berries.isafdar",
"White berries spawn in an isolated area in Isafdar, north of the Tirannwn lodestone and just west of some light animica rocks. They respawn very quickly (about 4-5 seconds) after being picked up.",
"Once there, just stand over the white berry spawn, clicking it whenever they spawn. After you've collected 28 of them, use the TokKul-Zo to bank, and repeat. Once you've got enough berries, sell them on the Grand Exchange.",
"It's also possible to use a Beast of Burden to increase the berries per trip.",
"As all you need to do is click once every few seconds, you can do other activities like High Level Alchemy or Disassemble on noted items while you wait.",
"Isafdar, Lletya",
"Partial completion of the quest Regicide is required to access Isafdar.",
"Tirannwn lodestone teleport is located in the south of Isafdar.",
"Use Tirannwn quiver 1, Crystal teleport seed, or Attuned crystal teleport seed to Lletya and then exit Lletya to the west into Isafdar.",
"Use Tirannwn quiver 2, 3, and 4 offer additional teleport locations around Isafdar — the Tyras Camp and the Elf Camp, respectively.",
"Use White berries spawn in an isolated area in Isafdar, north of the Tirannwn lodestone and just west of some light animica rocks. They respawn very quickly (about 4-5 seconds) after being picked up.",
"During Mourning's End Part I, Eluned will teleport you into the city for the first time and give you a crystal teleport seed with 8 charges that lets you teleport back to the city. She will also recharge it for a fee, though this amount goes down the more times you recharge the crystal with her, like with the crystal bow and crystal ward. Additional crystal teleport seeds can be obtained from killing the elves in the city, but they will only have three charges.",
"If a player chooses not to teleport into Lletya, there is an entrance from the forest of Isafdar, which is guarded by dire wolves. Trees surround the rest of the settlement, making it the only way out while walking or running.",
"Players who have completed The Prisoner of Glouphrie may take a safe path that begins near the Ourania Altar entrance, and takes them to the city itself. This path isn't really any shorter and due to the lack of maps of the area, may be more difficult than the other routes, but it can be used even if you have not yet begun the Mourning's End Part I quest. However, if you have not yet begun Mourning's End Part I, be careful who you talk to in the village. It is safe to talk to most of the elves, and to use the bank and shops, but if you speak to Arianwyn (and possibly some others), you will be transported out of the village because you don't belong there.",
"Players who have at least completed the easy Tirannwn achievements can use the Tirannwn quiver 1 to teleport to Lletya.",
"collecting-white-berries.red-dragon-isle",
"Red Dragon Isle",
"65 Attack",
"40 to wield the Wilderness sword and utilize Barge",
"Wilderness sword 1 for the Wilderness herb patch teleport",
"While not needed, unlocking Double Surge codex will aid in faster trips.",
"Mobile perk or Shadow's Grace recommended",
"52 recommended for use of Spirit terrorbird for longer trips.",
"54 for Red Dragon Isle shortcut",
"Utilising area loot and movement abilities, white berries may be collected at a faster volume than those found in Isafdar due to two berries spawning on Red Dragon Isle, though this may require more unlocks and attention.",
"It is highly recommended to assign a keybind to the area loot interface through the controls tab in your settings. By doing this, it is possible to spam the keybind in order to remove the slight delay it will take for the white berries to show in the area loot interface once they spawn, allowing for quicker trips.",
"It is also highly suggested to stand one tile south of the southern white berries spawn, as this will prevent the nearby burnt bones from appearing in your area loot interface and ensure both spawns of berries will.",
"Once your inventory and familiar are full, teleport to War's Retreat or use the Wilderness sword to teleport to Edgeville. Deposit your berries and return to the Wilderness herb patch once more.",
