"Royal dragonhide body",
"The rates assume 1800 bodies are made per hour with Portable crafters, Scroll of dexterity, Brooch of the Gods, Modified artisan's bandana and a Beast of Burden such as a Pack Yak along with bank presets to minimize banking time. This method is viable without any of these, but rates are lower. Each items effect to profits are marked at the end of the guide.",
"The player should make a preset of 18 threads and fill rest of the inventory and possible Beast of burden with Royal dragon leathers. It should take you 36 seconds to craft 18 royal dragonhide bodies (with banking). You should be able to craft 1800 royal dragonhide bodies an hour. All of the 1800 threads won't be needed because 1 thread may be used to craft multiple royal dragonhide bodies. With Crafting cape no threads are needed.",
"Lacking recommended and optional items affect profits as follows.",
"crafting-ruby-jewellery.rings-from-ores",
"Crafting ruby jewellery",
"Money making guide/Crafting ruby jewellery",
"Rings from ores",
"Ring mould (if not already on your tool belt)",
"Ruby rings are made by combining a gold bar and a cut ruby. It is highly recommended you make a bank preset with 28 rubies.",
"Smith all of the bars using your 28 ore (60 if you wearing smelting gauntlets), then use the rubies preset to craft the rings. Wearing Varrock armour 2 gives a chance to smelt 2 bars at once; the medium New Varrock achievements also have to be completed for this to apply at a portable forge or Lumbridge furnace.",
"The process is fairly click intensive, and very tedious. The crafting can be done at the Lumbridge furnace, across the street from the Lumbridge Market bank chest. It takes 9 seconds to travel between the bank and furnace.",
"One cycle costs 88 seconds for 28 bars and 69 seconds for 28 rings, for a total cycle time of 157 seconds (under 3 minutes per cycle).",
"Lumbridge furnace, across from the Lumbridge Market bank chest",
"crafting-sapphire-jewellery.necklaces",
"Crafting sapphire jewellery",
"Money making guide/Crafting sapphire jewellery",
"22 Crafting",
"Sapphire",
"Sapphire necklace",
"Sapphire necklaces are made by combining a gold bar and a sapphire. It is highly recommended you make a bank preset with 28 sapphires, which you can store gold bars in the metal bank.",
"The process is fairly click intensive, and very tedious. You'll need a furnace to craft the sapphire bracelets, this can be done at the Lumbridge furnace, across the street from the Lumbridge market bank chest.",
"crafting-soul-runes.with-catalytic-anima-stones",
"The numbers listed assumes using expansive pouch, the Infinity ethereal outfit, the Abyssal Titan, and running 5.4 trips per hour while using the Powerburst of sorcery and catalytic anima stones every time you go through the abyss. It also assumes that the player has Wilderness elite tasks complete for Magical thread as well as using urns with the urn enhancer.",
"crafting-soul-runes.without-catalytic-anima-stones",
"The numbers listed assumes using expansive pouch, the Infinity ethereal outfit, the Abyssal Titan, and running 5.4 trips per hour while using the Powerburst of sorcery every time you go through the abyss. It also assumes that the player has Wilderness elite tasks complete for Magical thread as well as using urns with the urn enhancer.",
"crafting-time-runes-through-the-abyss.standard",
"Crafting time runes through the Abyss",
"Money making guide/Crafting time runes through the Abyss",
"100 (105 for Expansive pouch and max level of Savvy runecrafting)",
"67 for Shadows grace",
"Runecrafting potion (any tier)",
"Powerburst of sorcery doubles the rune multiplier",
"Catalytic anima stone adds +2 the the rune multiplier",
"Runecrafting cape perk has an unknown chance to act as anima stones",
"The numbers listed assumes using expansive pouch, the Infinity ethereal outfit, and the Abyssal Titan, and running 90 trips per hour while using the powerburst of sorcery every fourth trip. The quantity of anima stones consumed per hour does not account for the Runecrafting cape perk activating (the cape acts as free anima stones, taking priority over the anima stones in the inventory).",
"With optimised dives and surges, one can expect around 92–109 trips an hour, while without using any mobility abilities, one can expect 73–83 trips an hour. Unlike most other methods of runecrafting using the abyss, it is better to not use the Nexus Mod relic here as it places you so far from the portal to the time altar. Going through the outer ring instead saves approximately 2 seconds per trip.",
"Load last preset from bank (manually load it the first time).",
"Time Altar",
"As with most other rune temples, it can be accessed via the Abyss. The time rift requires the ruins to be anchored using the enchanted key from Making History or the enchanted key from Meeting History at the time altar.",
"The fastest way to get there is through the Abyss with the Nexus Mod relic power and teleporting to Edgeville using the Wilderness sword.",
"A second way to get there is to use the North-western Anachronia Teleport spell or tablet. Harnessing the Abyssal Link relic power causes the spell to no longer require runes.",
"A third way to get there is to cast Anachronia Teleport if the Totem of the Abyss is placed on the totem pedestal on the north side of Anachronia.",
"crafting-water-runes-through-the-abyss.with-wild-runes",
"with Wild Runes",
"sprite_invention_icon_perks_tools_wild_runes",
"crafting-water-runes-through-the-abyss.without-wild-runes",
"without Wild Runes",
