"Small crate (classic components)",
"Using the bare minimum: Elder rune mattock and precision upgrade No. 2, while being AFK (99% activity time). Depending on your equipment and upgrades, can increase the artefacts per hour.",
"Buy 1,120 of each material from the GE. Use the Restore calc to determine how much you need depending on how many artefacts you gain per hour.",
"Disassemble the green dragonhide bodies (with Invention master cape worn or on the skillcape stand) by yourself, or put them in an Auto disassembler mk. II for idle components (larger quantities).",
"Excavate Venator remains to obtain artefacts.",
"Once you have obtained at least 80 in total, go to the workbench and restore them.",
"As it is hourly money making guide, it does not take into account the cost and time of collecting and disassembling the items into components.",
"creating-spirit-mementos.standard",
"Creating spirit mementos",
"Money making guide/Creating spirit mementos",
"Fragile memento",
"Spirit memento",
"Can be done every 4 hours; a run takes about 13 minutes.",
"Spirit mementos are needed for greater communion rituals in Necromancy. The main limiting factor of this money making method is the buy limit of 1,000 fragile mementos every 4 hours.",
"The player should make a bank preset of 90 vibrant energy and 27 fragile mementos. A full inventory can be converted in approximately 20 seconds.",
"crushing-desert-goat-horns.standard",
"Crushing desert goat horns",
"Money making guide/Crushing desert goat horns",
"Goat horn dust",
"Goat horn dust is an ingredient in the Combat potion and is the tertiary ingredient in infusing Smoke devil pouches. It is often profitable to crush the horns and sell them on the Grand Exchange. Like all methods involving large amounts of buying and selling, it is recommended to test the market first to make sure crushing the horns is profitable. Note that the Desert goat horn will often buy at under market price and the dust will occasionally sell at over market, so actual profits may be higher.",
"28 horns can be crushed per inventory, and each inventory can take from 16.8 to 20 seconds. Desert goat horns are crushed at 0.6 seconds per horn, so a maximum of around 5,000 horn can be ground per hour. Your rates may vary.",
"Please note that Desert goat horns have a buying limit of 10,000 every four hours.",
"Horns have very unstable prices/supply and the dust sells slowly.",
"cultivating-hydrangea-bushes-at-het-s-oasis.standard",
"Cultivating hydrangea bushes at Het's Oasis",
"Money making guide/Cultivating hydrangea bushes at Het's Oasis",
"70 Farming",
"99 Farming (recommended)",
"Hydrangeas",
"Using ultracompost will speed up harvesting which will allow up to 20 harvests an hour. There is a moneymaking guide on how do this here.",
"The drop rate for golden roses is 1/7 per harvest (tested with 100 harvests). Using these rates, and assuming the median of 2 golden roses per cultivation, 5 golden roses is an accurate estimate of profits.",
"Prices may vary",
"cutting-acadia-logs.variant-1",
"Variant 1",
"80 Woodcutting",
"Tier 7 Reputation for access to the VIP skilling area",
"Cadantine incense sticks",
"Splintering arrow tips",
"Optionally, the players could use signs of the porter to deposit the logs, making this a little more AFK, but cutting into the profits. Considering the close proximity of the bank chest, this is discouraged.",
"VIP skilling area",
"cutting-acadia-logs.variant-2",
"Variant 2",
"50 Woodcutting",
"Rune hatchet",
"Acadia wood box",
"Fire altar teleport (recommended)",
"Equip a usable hatchet and cut the acadia trees west of Het's Oasis. Bank the logs when you need more backpack space, then return to the trees.",
"West of Het's Oasis",
"Acadia tree",
"cutting-eternal-magic-logs.standard",
"Cutting eternal magic logs",
"Money making guide/Cutting eternal magic logs",
"100 Woodcutting",
"Hatchet (highest tier hatchet that you have)",
"Eternal magic wood box",
"The perfect juju woodcutting potion grants a 5% boost to logs gained and 1 dose is used per hour.",
"The Perfect plus potion grants the same buffs as the perfect juju woodcutting potion but lasts for 4 hours instead.",
"cutting-granite.standard",
"Cutting granite",
"Money making guide/Cutting granite",
"Assumes the guide's 1,800 actions per hour. Adjust it to your own pace.",
"Granite is the tertiary ingredient for granite lobster familiars, and while any size granite can be used for this, the 500 gram pieces are the cheapest and most in demand. Buy some Granite (2kg) on the Grand Exchange (they are sometimes difficult to purchase), and withdraw seven of them at a time. Craft the granite into 500 gram pieces, bank, and repeat. Each load takes about 12 seconds, so cutting around 2,000 pieces of granite per hour can be expected. Using a bank preset can speed up the process drastically and is recommended.",
"Grand Exchange recommended",
"cutting-jade.standard",
"Cutting jade",
"Money making guide/Cutting jade",
"13 Crafting",
"50 Crafting (recommended)",
"Chisel",
"An uncut jade can be cut with a chisel by a player with level 13 Crafting, and grants the player 20 Crafting experience. However, there is a chance that the player will accidentally crush it to form a crushed gem, which gives only 5 Crafting experience. This chance decreases with a higher Crafting level, and stops completely at level 50.",
"The Grand Exchange buy limit is 5,000, so if a player plans on doing the activity for multiple hours continuously they will need to buy more in advance.",
"cutting-logs.standard",
"Cutting logs",
"Money making guide/Cutting logs",
"1 Woodcutting",
"Adamant hatchet or better",
"Wood box or higher recommended",
"31 Woodcutting (recommended)",
"Seer's headband 1 (recommended)",
"Guam incense sticks (recommended)",
"Teleport to Port Sarim lodestone and start chopping all of the regular trees in the area. When your inventory is full, run north-east onto the docks and bank the logs. This should take about three minutes per load of 28 logs with a decent Woodcutting level, so you may be able to cut more than 500 logs per hour. When finished, sell the logs on the Grand Exchange. Any seer's headband will double logs received from cutting a tree, and double your profit.",
"Guam incense sticks, which give the player a 10-40% chance of cutting an extra log depending on the incense stick's potency, are recommended. Cadantine incense sticks, which have a base 2.5% chance of not exhausting a tree, could be a useful secondary incense effect.",
"The evil tree buff temporarily removes the need to bank logs and makes trees last longer, although it may be better spent on higher level trees such as mahogany or acadia, which would provide much better experience with a medium decrease in profit.",
"Port Sarim recommended",
"Players can teleport to Port Sarim using the Home Teleport spell once they have activated Port Sarim lodestone.",
"Port Sarim can be entered by land from Falador to the north/north-west, Draynor Village to the east, Rimmington to the west, or Thurgo's Peninsula to the south.",
"If a player has the explorer's ring 3 or 4 equipped or in their inventory, they can teleport to the Falador cabbage patch north of the area and walk south.",
"Players can also travel by ship from Karamja, Crandor, or Entrana, arriving at the dock.",
"Teleport to Port Sarim lodestone and start chopping all of the regular trees in the area. When your inventory is full, run north-east onto the docks and bank the logs. This should take about three minutes per load of 28 logs with a decent Woodcutting level, so you may be able to cut more than 500 logs per hour. When finished, sell the logs on the Grand Exchange.",
"cutting-mahogany-logs.standard",
"Cutting mahogany logs",
"Money making guide/Cutting mahogany logs",
"Dragon hatchet, Crystal hatchet or Imcando hatchet",
"Wood box highest tier recommended",
"Deadliest Catch recommended for deposit box",
"60 (higher recommended)",
"33 recommended",
"22 recommended",
"God banner",
"Nature's sentinel outfit recommended",
"Honed perk",
"Jungle spiders, poisonous jungle snakes and poisonous scorpions found throughout the jungle. Wearing a monkey greegree will keep the monsters from attacking, but it also takes up an inventory space for your hatchet unless the hatchet is stored on the tool belt. These monsters can be completely avoided if you run along the southern edge of the island in a direct line from the mahogany tree to the deposit chest.",
"There is approximately a 2.5% chance that you will cut a Special mahogany log. You can use two of these to convert an inventory of mahogany logs into mahogany planks, saving 19,500 coins per special log. On average you will get about ten of these per hour, which means you can convert 130 logs for free by talking to the sawmill operator. It takes about 40 seconds to turn a batch of logs into planks, which can be done at any time after amassing enough special mahogany logs.",
"Travelling via Daero at the floor 1 above ground of the Grand Tree (east next to Blurberry), then talking to Waydar who will take you to Crash Island, and then sailing to Ape Atoll by talking to Lumdo.",
"Use the teleportation spell Ape Atoll Teleport, requiring level 64 Magic (after completing the King Awowogei part of Recipe for Disaster).",
"Teleporting to the Agility course using the fairy ring code CLR (after completing A Fairy Tale III - Battle at Ork's Rift). A small ninja monkey greegree is required to get through the log shortcut to the agility course and the rest of the island.",
"Superior locator Special log teleport (1/8 chance, requires visiting Ape Atoll once, during Monkey Madness).",
"A completed nature's sentinel outfit boosts woodcutting speed by 7% and also offers 20 daily teleports to tree locations.",
