"enchanting-onyx-bolts.standard",
"Enchanting onyx bolts",
"Money making guide/Enchanting onyx bolts",
"87 Magic",
"Onyx bolts",
"The Enchant Crossbow Bolt (Onyx) spell enchants 10 bolts at a time, using one cosmic rune, one death rune and 20 fire runes. Use a staff of fire for free fire runes. Click the Enchant Crossbow Bolt magic spell, which opens a menu to enchant bolts. 60 sets of 10 bolts can be made using the menu, taking approximately 142 seconds. This gives a theoretical upper limit of 15,000 enchanted Onyx bolts per hour. As all inputs and outputs are stackable, there is no requirement to bank and this technique can be done anywhere.",
"The bolt market is fairly volatile, so test the profit of one set of bolts before you buy the runes and bolts in bulk. Maximise your profit by buying one Onyx bolt (e) instantly, and sell all of yours for slightly less than what you paid. They may take a while to sell, but an extra 100 coins per bolt can double your profit.",
"excavating-castra-debris.standard",
"Excavating Castra debris",
"Money making guide/Excavating Castra debris",
"Breaking the seal",
"Castra debris are found south of the entrance in Kharid-et Dig Site. Just next to the prison door.",
"Your actual profit may be higher or lower depending on your drop rates, and intensity.",
"excavating-tsutsaroth-remains.standard",
"Excavating Tsutsaroth remains",
"Money making guide/Excavating Tsutsaroth remains",
"Excavate Tsutsaroth remains and destroy artefacts while selling all material gained. Only need to click about once every 7 minutes if you have the 10 minutes auto logout so that it starts a new artefact. Profit could be increased using anything that makes you use fewer signs of the porter, an XP capacitor, or a waterfiend familiar if desired. Did not calculate for charge usage, but it is fairly low for this method. You will want honed 6 on your mattock to get 1000+ materials per hour at 120 arch. If you click the next artefact quickly you can get more than 1000 materials per hour - this is a conservative estimate. 116 Archaeology required, but 120 will yield more material as will using Ring of Whispers to boost Arch level. On the recommended items list, each item missing will mean fewer materials per hour. Guide is calculated based on having all those items except for the waterfiend.",
"Tsutsaroth remains, Infernal Source Dig Site",
"excavating-venator-remains.standard",
"Excavating Venator remains",
"Money making guide/Excavating Venator remains",
"Venator remains are found just east of Al Kharid. This assumes level 20 Archaeology and following time sprites.",
"This is similar to excavating Third Age iron, which is usually more profitable, but venator remains cannot be depleted and there is no competition between players.",
"Screening ancient gravel can be very profitable, but is less so in free-to-play due to various limitations.",
"excavating-xolo-remains.standard",
"Excavating Xolo remains",
"Money making guide/Excavating Xolo remains",
"119 Archaeology",
"Excavate Xolo remains and destroy artefacts while selling all material gained. You only need to click about once every 7.5 minutes if you have the 10 minutes auto logout so that it starts a new artefact. Profit could be increased using anything that makes you use less signs of the porter, an XP Capacitor 5000, or a waterfiend familiar if desired. Did not calculate for charge usage, but it is fairly low for this method and is also partially offset if you use the perk Imp Souled. You will want Honed 6 on your mattock to get 1100+ materials per hour at 120 arch. If you click the next artefact quickly, you can acquire more than 1100 materials per hour. This is a conservative estimate. 116 Archaeology required, but 120 will yield more material as will using Ring of Whispers to boost Archaeology level. On the recommended items list each item missing will mean less materials per hour. Guide is calculated based on having all those items except for the waterfiend.",
"excavating-material-cache-blood-of-orcus.standard",
"Excavating material cache (Blood of Orcus)",
"Money making guide/Excavating material cache (Blood of Orcus)",
"Rune mattock or better",
"Assumes the guide's 400 actions per hour. Adjust it to your own pace.",
"Profits will be affected by the level of mattock used. To increase profit further players can use a mattock with perks such as Honed and Fortune. Using perks such as Imp Souled or Refined may reduce the usage of porter charges and the need to world hop. If owned the master archaeologist's outfit grants a 7% increased excavation rate; a ring of Whispers can invisibly boost Archaeology by 3 levels to increase excavation rate and the waterfiend familiar has the effect of doubling resources 5% of the time when gathering.",
"Kharid-Et Dig Site- Chapel Excavation Site",
"excavating-material-cache-stormguard-steel.standard",
"Excavating material cache (Stormguard steel)",
"Money making guide/Excavating material cache (Stormguard steel)",
"70 Archaeology",
"76 Archaeology (recommended)",
"Dragon mattock (recommended)",
"Excavation rates are based on near minimum level and non-augmented dragon mattock. Upgrades may significantly increase profit.",
"Stormguard steel can be excavated from material cache (Stormguard steel). There is a materials cart close by in the Stormguard Citadel Dig Site. Assuming you have unlocked 250 capacity for the archaeological soil box, it takes about 100 minutes for a full trip. World hopping is necessary as the caches deplete faster than they respawn (2 minutes).",
"excavating-material-cache-third-age-iron.standard",
"Excavating material cache (Third Age iron)",
"Money making guide/Excavating material cache (Third Age iron)",
"Third Age iron can be excavated from material cache (Third Age iron), with 3 caches north-east of the Archaeology Campus. With a bank a short distance to the west, each trip of 28 materials takes around 6 minutes on an empty world. Each cache usually gives multiples of the material before depleting, and it is shared among players.",
"excavating-material-cache-cadmium-red.standard",
"Excavating material cache (cadmium red)",
"Money making guide/Excavating material cache (cadmium red)",
"24 Archaeology",
"Archaeological soil box recommended",
"Excavate the material cache (cadmium red) in the Star Lodge cellar at the Infernal Source Dig Site until it is depleted, hopping worlds each time it does so until the backpack is full. Bank it in the bank chest above the dig site and repeat.",
"It is highly recommended to use a soil box so as to increase the amount of cadmium red that can be excavated in a single inventory.",
"Star Lodge cellar, Infernal Source Dig Site",
"excavating-material-cache-cobalt-blue.standard",
"Excavating material cache (cobalt blue)",
"Money making guide/Excavating material cache (cobalt blue)",
"48 Archaeology",
"Adamant mattock or better",
"Excavate material cache (cobalt blue) at the Everlight Dig Site until it is depleted, hopping worlds each time it does so until the backpack is full. Deposit materials at the materials cart near the cache and repeat.",
"It is highly recommended to use a soil box so as to increase the amount of cobalt blue that can be excavated in a single inventory.",
