"Farming master cape (recommended)",
"1000 scarabs caught and bought Double loot and Flower saving chance from Dundee's Crocodile Upgrades",
"Rapid Growth can be used once (twice with the full master farmer outfit) every day on all four flower patches in Het's Oasis, making them instantly harvestable. When you harvest flowers at Het's Oasis, you get a chance to harvest golden roses. Using compost on the plant before cultivating it increases this chance, with better compost giving a higher chance. These roses can be used to catch dazzling whirligigs, whose shells can be ground into powder of penance.",
"generating-compost-with-a-compost-mound-familiar.normal-account",
"Generating compost with a compost mound familiar",
"Money making guide/Generating compost with a compost mound familiar",
"Normal account",
"28 Summoning",
"WOLF_WHISTLE",
"Wolf Whistle",
"Buckets All the Way Down upgrade from Sydekix's Shop of Balance",
"Compost mound pouch",
"Compost Mound scroll (Generate Compost)",
"Compost",
"It's recommended to complete this method in Taverley, just north of the Player-owned house portal, where the Tool leprechaun stands right next to the compost bin. The tool leprechaun at this location will also never move from his position. Each use of the scroll requires 12 special move points, which regenerate back normally in slightly less than 22 seconds, allowing the player to use approximately 167 scrolls per hour without the use of any special move boosting effects. A compost mound familiar lasts 36 minutes without any extensions.",
"Buckets All the Way Down upgrade allows players to draw compost from the compost bin without requiring any buckets, and is therefore ultimately required for maximum profit and uptime. This can be bought at Sydekix's Shop of Balance for 10,000 Crux Eqal favour.",
"When the special move bar is regenerating, you should take compost from the bin and right-click 'Exchange' with the tool leprechaun to store all the compost with him, you may then right click the stored buckets to withdraw them in noted form at any point. The compost bin will hold a maximum of 1000 processed compost of each type, so it is not possible to do an entire hour without drawing any buckets from the bin.",
"grinding-sandstone-into-extra-fine-sand.standard",
"Grinding sandstone into extra fine sand",
"Money making guide/Grinding sandstone into extra fine sand",
"20 Crafting",
"This method requires you to grind 10kg blocks of sandstone into extra fine sand. Including banking time, a full inventory should take about 36 seconds and yield an average of 28 extra fine sand.",
"Although the Crafting experience gained is minimal, it can be boosted by wearing the artisan's outfit and wise perk, and experience can be nearly doubled by using a magic carpet pet and Shadow-touched training set.",
"Extra fine sand is an item used in the creation of the Orthen furnace core and blessed sand, the latter of which is used during the creation of an artificer's measure or a blessed flask. Because of this, there is moderate demand for this item.",
"harvesting-elder-energy.standard",
"Harvesting elder energy",
"Money making guide/Harvesting elder energy",
"75 Divination",
"Elder energy is usually in demand for those who want the extra Divination experience from converting memories with energy or to be used to create nightmare muspah and Nihil familiars. 75 Divination, and completion of Fate of the Gods is required to harvest elder energy. 81 Summoning for a Nightmare muspah familiar will also increase the amount of energy and sharply reduce trips to the rift for convertion, while the Divine Conversion power allows you to instantly convert an inventory of memories. Remember that in order for an enriched wisp to spawn, players must empower the rift with the elder chronicles that they collect, which grant their normal experience reward while doing so. Harvest the enriched wisp for a guaranteed supply of enriched memories. Enriched memories can be converted to twice the energy that normal memories can.",
"For maximum profit, convert all memories into energy (option one). Converting memories to energy produces energies at approximately 16,000 per hour with a Muspah. If better experience gain is desired, players can convert their memories into experience (option two) instead.",
"Without a Nightmare Muspah, energy per hour is down to only 14,900.",
"After completing Fate of the Gods, use the World Gate set to Freneskae to reach the Elder Halls. The elder divination outfit can also teleport to the elder wisp colony.",
"harvesting-incandescent-energy.with-divine-o-matic-vacuum",
"With Divine-o-matic vacuum",
"101 (or 95 and 84 with Extreme invention)",
"Divine-o-matic vacuum",
"South of the Poison Waste",
"As part of Tirannwn, accessing the Poison Waste requires completion of the Underground Pass quest.",
"The system of islands can be accessed by jumping on rocks on the north-east side of the waste, south-west of Lletya. From Lletya, pass the tree and then run directly south to get to the rocks.",
"The Tirannwn lodestone is located directly north of the Poison Waste.",
"The Tirannwn quiver 3 and its upgrade can teleport the player to the Tirannwn mushroom patch, which is located nearby.",
"harvesting-incandescent-energy.without-divine-o-matic-vacuum",
"Without Divine-o-matic vacuum",
"The World Wakes for Divine conversion",
"Having unlocked the Divine Conversion relic for Divine Conversion",
"98 recommended for Divine Conversion, even with a memory dowser",
"86 recommended (boostable from 81 with Super invention or from 69 with Extreme invention) for Divine Conversion",
"Memory dowser (recommended)",
"Poison Waste Swamp",
"harvesting-luminous-energy.standard",
"Harvesting luminous energy",
"Money making guide/Harvesting luminous energy",
"93 Divination (recommended)",
"Sliske's Endgame (recommended)",
"Turned in a completed memory-storage bot (Cres) to the Archivist",
"Luminous energy is usually in demand for those who want the extra Divination experience from converting memories with energy, or those who want to train Invention. Level 90 Divination is required to harvest luminous energy, but having level 93 gives the best chances of harvesting enriched luminous memories. Remember that in order for an enriched wisp to spawn, players must empower the rift with the chronicle fragments that they collect, which grant their normal experience reward while doing so. Harvest it for a guaranteed supply of enriched memories. Enriched memories can be converted to twice the energy that normal memories can.",
"an elder divination outfit provides a 7% chance to harvest double memories and energy at once, and a 5% chance to harvest five times the normal memory from a wisp.",
"a nightmare muspah familiar gives a 3% passive boost towards finding enriched memories and has a 5% chance to obtain four times the energy from wisps.",
"South of Sophanem",
