"1 Divination",
"5 Divination (recommended)",
"Pale energy",
"Pale energy is usually in demand for those who create divine charges or augmentors. Level 1 Divination is required to harvest pale energy, but having level 5 gives a small increase in the amount of converted pale energy per pale memory.",
"For maximum profit, convert all memories into energy (the first option). Converting memories to energy produces energies at approximately 2,273 per hour.",
"harvesting-radiant-energy.standard",
"Harvesting radiant energy",
"Money making guide/Harvesting radiant energy",
"85 Divination",
"Radiant energy is usually in demand for those who want the extra Divination experience from converting memories with energy. 85 Divination is required to harvest radiant energy, but having level 90 gives the best chances of harvesting enriched radiant memories. Remember that in order for an enriched wisp to spawn, players must empower the rift with the chronicle fragments that they collect, which grant their normal experience reward while doing so. Harvest the enriched wisp for a guaranteed supply of enriched memories. Enriched memories can be converted to twice the energy that normal memories can.",
"99 Divination.",
"Elder divination outfit.",
"Divination cape.",
"Charter a ship to Port Phasmatys, or teleport using ectophial, then speak with the ghost captain standing next to a small row boat at the southern end of the docks. Ghostspeak amulet or completion of the hard Morytania achievements required. The Ghosts Ahoy quest does not have to be started for him to take the player there, but it is required for the ectophial.",
"Big Book o' Piracy teleport directly to the island (requires completion of Pieces of Hate).",
"Elder divination outfit can teleport its owner to the wisp colony three times each day.",
"harvesting-vibrant-energy.standard",
"Harvesting vibrant energy",
"Money making guide/Harvesting vibrant energy",
"98 (boostable from 96 with cup of soil tea)",
"86 (boostable from 81 with super invention potion or from 69 with extreme invention potion)",
"Having unlocked the Divine Conversion relic from Archaeology",
"80 Divination (recommended)",
"Divination cape (recommended)",
"Ethereal Connection and Wisp Herder buffs from Memorial to Guthix recommended",
"Vibrant energy is in demand for creating Sign of the porter IV. It is also useful for those who want the extra Divination experience from converting memories with energy and for creating Divine box traps. 60 Divination is required to harvest vibrant energy, but having level 75 gives the best chances of harvesting enriched vibrant memories and gives 3 energy per harvest. Remember that in order for an enriched wisp to spawn, players must empower the rift with the chronicle fragments that they collect, which grant their normal experience reward while doing so. Harvest it for a guaranteed supply of enriched memories. Enriched memories can be converted to twice the energy that normal memories can.",
"With level 98 Archaeology and 86 Invention, the player can unlock the Divine Conversion relic, which allows the conversion of a whole inventory of memories in one go.",
"Use the South Feldip Hills Teleport.",
"Teleport with a ring of duelling to the Warforge Dig Site.",
"Teleport by using the Archaeology Guild map, using the Archaeology teleport or the master archaeologist's outfit to teleport to the Warforge Dig Site.",
"Additionally the Elder divination outfit can be used to teleport to the vibrant wisp colony.",
"havenhythe-big-game-hunter.chinchompas",
"Chinchompas",
"Assumes the guide's 25 actions per hour. Adjust it to your own pace.",
"Giant chinchompas take slightly longer to kill, however the meat obtained is more valuable potentially offering larger profits. The quantities of apex hide and raw giant chinchompa meat stated here assume that giant golden chinchompas are hunted.",
"havenhythe-big-game-hunter.kebbits",
"Kebbits",
"98 Hunter",
"Assumes the guide's 35 actions per hour. Adjust it to your own pace.",
"Giant kebbits can be hunted faster than their chinchompa counterparts allowing for more meat and hides to be gathered in the same amount of time. The quantities of apex hide and raw giant kebbit meat stated here assume that giant dashing kebbits are hunted.",
"high-level-player-owned-farm-run.standard",
"High level player-owned farm run",
"Money making guide/High level player-owned farm run",
"Raw tuna",
"Woad leaf",
"Gloomshroom zygomite",
"Crystal chinchompa",
"Zygomite fruit",
"mort myre fungus",
"Chinchompa residue",
"Can be done every 42 hours; a run takes about 5 minutes.",
"Black dragon eggs can be bought from the Grand Exchange and can reliably be sold to other players at the adolescent stage for 400,000-450,000 coins, Unchecked zygomites can be bought from the Grand Exchange and can reliably be sold to other players at the adolescent stage for 200,000-250,000 coins, unchecked crystal chinchompas can be bought from the Grand Exchange and can reliably be sold to other players at the adolescent stage for 70,000-90,000 coins.",
"The output can be other types of zygomites and chinchompas.",
"These animals are removed from the pen and replaced with an egg/child/sporeling at the adolescent age due to the quantity of beans received from selling each animal to its individual NPC buyer. The quantity is highest at this age, so players looking to buy animals to exchange for beans will be more likely to buy the best return on their own investment.",
"In order to reduce investment costs, players may choose to spend a little extra time at the Manor Farm on a populated and/or trade dedicated world and buy \"checked\" versions of first stage animals from other players for a much lower price than \"(unchecked)\" counterparts via the Grand Exchange. Keeping in mind that once checked, farm animals do not stack in the bank. Purchasing the storm barn and subsequent extensions allows for up to 60 checked animals to be stored outside of the bank.",
"humidifying-vials.standard",
"Humidifying vials",
"Money making guide/Humidifying vials",
"68 Magic",
"Lunar spells as active spellbook in order to cast Humidify (Lunar Diplomacy)",
"Vials of water are often in high demand because they must be used with a herb in order to make an unfinished potion. Players often buy them in bulk.",
"One can cast Humidify on an inventory of vials. Use astral runes and equip a steam battlestaff to maximise profit and efficiency. Set up one of your \"Quick Presets\" to Withdraw 27 vials and an astral rune, cast the Humidify spell, which will cause the whole inventory to fill vials with water, open the bank, click the quick preset and repeat. When playing at maximum efficiency, up to 400 spells can be cast per hour, for 10,800 vials of water.",
"Vials have a buy limit of 10,000 every 4 hours and it is not often that they will buy for 1 coin. Decanting plenty of potions is a fast way of obtaining vials. To decant, bring as many 3 or 4 dose potions to Bob Barter and select \"Decant\" and select \"1 dose\" (make sure there are no empty vials). He will charge 2 coins for each vial. Then select the \"Decant\" option from him and he will turn back all the potions to \"4 dose\" then bank the excess vials. Repeat the same process as many times as possible. It is recommended to buy cheaper potions if you do not own plenty of potions.",
