"making-ghostly-ink.regular",
"making-guam-potions.standard",
"Making guam potions",
"Money making guide/Making guam potions",
"907,200 +recommended",
"Clean guam",
"Guam potion (unfinished)",
"Guam potion (unfinished) are used to create attack potions. Players can avoid the tedium of making unfinished potions and buy them directly from the Grand Exchange. This opens up an opportunity to make unfinished guam potions for profit. Before buying the ingredients in bulk, make sure that the method is profitable by making one unfinished potion and testing the profit.",
"Creating a preset loadout with 14 clean guam and 14 vials of water. Using preset loadouts will help speed up the number of unfinished potions per hour by reducing the intermediary steps; depositing your unfinished potions and withdrawing 14 herbs and vials. Each inventory should take about 21 seconds with banking, which means you can make around 2,400 potions per hour.",
"making-infernal-magic-incense-sticks.standard",
"Making infernal magic incense sticks",
"Money making guide/Making infernal magic incense sticks",
"Quick-cense more than doubles the rate of creating incense sticks",
"Assumes the guide's 2,600 actions per hour. Adjust it to your own pace.",
"Withdraw magic incense sticks and infernal ashes. Combine one stick with two infernal ashes to make one infernal magic incense stick.",
"Bank the finished sticks, refill the supplies and repeat. Quick-cense increases production speed if unlocked.",
"making-infernal-urns.standard",
"Making infernal urns",
"Money making guide/Making infernal urns",
"Infernal urn (no rune)",
"The result may differ from player to player.",
"The urns can be made by going to the Crafting guild and making them at the Potter's wheel. After that, go to the Potter's oven and turn them into Infernal urn (no rune). They can then be deposited in the nearby bank deposit box (or bank chest if hard Falador achievements have been completed). You can combine mining clay and making soft clay to earn more profit.",
"Portable crafters are recommended for their 10% chance of saving clay and 10% chance of saving unfired urns.",
"Crafting guild",
"A skills necklace or modified artisan's bandana can be used to teleport to the Crafting Guild.",
"Teleport to the Port Sarim lodestone and running north-west.",
"Teleport to the Rimmington player-owned house portal.",
"Members who have unlocked the Crafting Guild hot air balloon route after completing Enlightened Journey can take a hot air balloon to just north of the Crafting Guild for a fee of two charges.",
"The urns can be made by going to the Crafting guild and making them at the Potter's wheel. After that, go to the Potter's oven and turn them into Infernal urn (no rune). They can then be deposited in the nearby bank deposit box (or bank chest if hard Falador achievements have been completed).",
"making-large-historic-component-crates.standard",
"Making large historic component crates",
"Money making guide/Making large historic component crates",
"20 Invention",
"70 Archaeology (recommended)",
"Auto-screener v1.080 recommended for faster screening and less hassle",
"Grace of the elves or Sign of the porter VII recommended for less banking",
"Master archaeologist's hat (recommended)",
"Luck of the Dwarves recommended (or other tier 4 luck item)",
"Honed recommended, rank 6 for 12% (13.2%) increased materials",
"Hasty recommended, rank 5 for 10% (11%) increased artefacts per hour",
"sprite_invention_icon_perks_tools_hasty",
"Preservationist recommended, rank 5 for 5% (5.5%) of artefacts automatically restored for no materials",
"sprite_invention_icon_perks_tools_preservationist",
"Flow State relic power recommended for 20% precision (more artefacts per hour)",
"Augmented mattock",
"Padded parts",
"Protective components",
"Timeworn components",
"Vintage components",
"Assumes the guide's 63 actions per hour. Adjust it to your own pace.",
"You can use Calculator:Archaeology/Hotspot to figure out how many artefacts per hour you can dig up. Disable \"Hide low level excavations?\" so you can see the venator remains hotspot and enable \"Stats for Nerds\" to see the artefacts rate. Multiply by 50 or 60 to give yourself 10 minutes to restore artefacts, disassemble items and create the crates.",
"In this method you create signs of the porter in an amount sufficient for upkeep of an hour, gathering of artefacts from venator remains in the Kharid-et Dig Site (starting from level 5). Then repair the artefacts and disassemble them, followed by disassembling items for protective components and padded parts, to create a large crate (historic components).",
"This method uses Excavating Venator remains as a basis, however instead of selling the materials, you will be repairing the artefacts venator dagger and venator light crossbow to get historical, classic, timeworn, and vintage components from their disassembly.",
"The auto-screener v1.080 will automatically turn all potential ancient gravel into Third Age iron and Zarosian insignia with a 50/50 chance. This will often increase your monetary yield compared to sifting the ancient gravel, as it can also award many other items - see Money making guide/Screening ancient gravel for comparison.",
"making-magic-incense-sticks.standard",
"Making magic incense sticks",
"Money making guide/Making magic incense sticks",
"An inventory of 28 magic logs can be crafted into 14 magic incense sticks. This can be done at any bank. Setting a bank preset to be 28 magic logs can make the banking process slightly easier. Magic logs can only be obtained by members, and magic incense sticks can only be used by members, but free players can simply buy magic logs at the Grand Exchange, process and resell the sticks. It takes 42 seconds to process 28 Magic logs, so a full load of 2000 will take at least 3024 seconds, or 50 minutes.",
