"Should Botanist's amulet be a positive number then using it will lose you money and therefore you shouldn't use it.",
"making-torstol-incense-sticks.standard",
"Making torstol incense sticks",
"Money making guide/Making torstol incense sticks",
"Torstol incense sticks are used by wealthy players for their global experience boost. While it would technically be faster to use infernal magic incense sticks in the process, there is no profit margin for whoever makes those, and as such they will hardly ever be found on the Grand Exchange. It takes 5 ticks to apply the ashes to the sticks, then 6 ticks to apply the herb to the ashed sticks. Accounting for some extra time for banking, 500 ashed and herbed incense sticks per hour is a reasonable expectation.",
"The Prayer experience from ashing the magic incense sticks is identical to the experience from scattering the infernal ashes, but unlike typical Prayer and Firemaking training methods, incense turns the logs and ashes into a sellable product rather than simply being destroyed, making it a rare method of training either skill that can actually make money in the process. It is slower Prayer XP than scattering the ashes due to the time required per ash and about half the time being taken up with applying the herb instead, to say nothing of using altars for Prayer training, but it is Prayer XP at a profit nonetheless.",
"making-ultracompost.standard",
"Making ultracompost",
"Money making guide/Making ultracompost",
"Plague's End (for maximum production)",
"With Infernus pyroclasts tradeable on the Grand Exchange, ultracompost production is no longer limited by the manure dropping rate of dragons at the Anachronia dinosaur farm. There are 7 compost bins, allowing for 105 buckets of ultracompost roughly every 90 minutes, effectively 70 buckets an hour. Compost bin locations: Manor Farm, Catherby, Taverley, South Falador, East of Canifis, Herblore Habitat, and Prifddinas.",
"making-ultracompost-infernus-pyroclasts.standard",
"Making ultracompost (infernus pyroclasts)",
"Money making guide/Making ultracompost (infernus pyroclasts)",
"50 required to access the Sydekix's Shop of Balance",
"Buckets All the Way Down unlocked from Sydekix's Shop of Balance",
"Can be done every 28 hours; a run takes about 20 minutes.",
"28 hours",
"With the release of Garden of Kharid, the process for making compost has been streamlined.",
"Deposit 1,000 noted infernus pyroclasts into any compost bin.",
"Return after about 28 hours to collect the ultracompost and deposit it to a tool leprechaun until the compost bin is empty.",
"A quick way to do this while avoiding the UI is to \"use\" the ultracompost on the leprechaun, typing in any number 28 or above (99 works) into the prompt and hitting enter.",
"Withdraw the ultracompost from the tool leprechaun in noted form (via the \"Noted-X\" option in the storage interface) and sell it.",
"Due to the game health update on 14 July 2025, prices may be unstable.",
"making-unfinished-avantoe-potions.standard",
"Making unfinished avantoe potions",
"Money making guide/Making unfinished avantoe potions",
"Avantoe potion (unfinished)",
"Avantoe potion (unfinished) are used to create super energy potions. Because these are often used to train Herblore, and adding clean avantoe to a vial of water gives little experience, many players avoid the tedium of making unfinished potions and buy them directly from the Grand Exchange.",
"making-unfinished-dwarf-weed-potions.standard",
"Making unfinished dwarf weed potions",
"Money making guide/Making unfinished dwarf weed potions",
"70 Herblore",
"Dwarf weed potion (unfinished)",
"Dwarf weed potion (unfinished) are used to create super ranging potions. Because these are often used to train Herblore, and adding clean dwarf weed to a vial of water gives little experience, many players avoid the tedium of making unfinished potions and buy them directly from the Grand Exchange. It is possible to obtain rates of up to 2800 potions per hour by using a beast of burden such as a pack yak along with bank presets to optimize time spent potion making. This will require a higher intensity in order to manage both inventories.",
"Using portable wells gives a 5% chance of making an extra potion, Brooch of the Gods gives an additional 5%, and the Modified botanist's mask gives another 5%. The scroll of cleansing gives a permanent 10% chance of not using up an ingredient when making potions. The bonuses of these items increase the number of unfinished potions you can make, and the portable well also makes the process less click-intensive. With a portable well placed next to a bank chest, click on the bank chest and deposit your inventory and withdraw 14 herbs and 14 vials of water by using a bank preset, and repeat.",
"Using portable wells gives a 5% chance of making an extra potion, Brooch of the Gods gives an additional 5%, and the Modified botanist's mask gives another 5%. The bonuses of these items increase the number of unfinished potions you can make, and the portable well also makes the process less click-intensive. With a portable well placed next to a bank chest, click on the bank chest and deposit your inventory and withdraw 14 herbs and 14 vials of water by using a bank preset, and repeat.",
"There is usually a portable well placed and maintained by someone else next to the bank chest in Fort Forinthry in world 84. However, if there isn't one and no-one else provides one within a reasonable amount of time, you may have to use your own wells.",
"making-unfinished-fellstalk-potions.standard",
"Making unfinished fellstalk potions",
"Money making guide/Making unfinished fellstalk potions",
"Fellstalk potion (unfinished)",
"Fellstalk potion (unfinished) are used to create Prayer renewals. Because these are often used to train Herblore, and adding clean fellstalk to a vial of water gives little experience, many players avoid the tedium of making unfinished potions and buy them directly from the Grand Exchange.",
"making-unfinished-irit-potions.standard",
"Making unfinished irit potions",
"Money making guide/Making unfinished irit potions",
"Irit potion (unfinished) are used to create super attack potions, and ultimately overload potions. Super attack and overload potions are a good method of training Herblore, as well as needed for high-level combat. While irit potion (unfinished)s are very useful, they are also incredibly tedious to make and do not give meaningful Herblore experience, causing many players to purchase them instead.",
"making-unfinished-kwuarm-potions.standard",
"Making unfinished kwuarm potions",
"Money making guide/Making unfinished kwuarm potions",
"Kwuarm potion (unfinished) are used to create super strength and weapon poisons. Because antifires are often used to train Herblore, and adding clean kwuarm to a vial of water gives little experience, many players avoid the tedium of making unfinished potions and buy them directly from the Grand Exchange.",
"making-unfinished-lantadyme-potions.standard",
"Making unfinished lantadyme potions",
"Money making guide/Making unfinished lantadyme potions",
"67 Herblore",
"Lantadyme potion (unfinished)",
"Lantadyme potion (unfinished) are used to create antifire and super magic potions. Because antifires are often used to train Herblore, and adding clean lantadyme to a vial of water gives little experience, many players avoid the tedium of making unfinished potions and buy them directly from the Grand Exchange.",
"making-unfinished-ranarr-potions.standard",
"Making unfinished ranarr potions",
"Money making guide/Making unfinished ranarr potions",
"Ranarr potion (unfinished) are used to create Prayer potions. Because these are often used to train Herblore, and adding clean ranarr to a vial of water gives little experience, many players avoid the tedium of making unfinished potions and buy them directly from the Grand Exchange. This opens up an opportunity to make unfinished ranarr potions for profit.",
"making-unfinished-snapdragon-potions.standard",
"Making unfinished snapdragon potions",
"Money making guide/Making unfinished snapdragon potions",
"Snapdragon potion (unfinished)",
"Snapdragon potion (unfinished) are used to create super restores. Because these are often used to train Herblore, and adding clean snapdragon to a vial of water gives little experience, many players avoid the tedium of making unfinished potions and buy them directly from the Grand Exchange.",
"making-unfinished-spirit-weed-potions.standard",
"Making unfinished spirit weed potions",
"Money making guide/Making unfinished spirit weed potions",
"Spirit weed potion (unfinished) are used to create summoning potions. While the unfinished potions are very useful, they are also tedious to make and do not give meaningful Herblore experience, causing many players to purchase them instead.",
"making-unfinished-toadflax-potions.standard",
"Making unfinished toadflax potions",
"Money making guide/Making unfinished toadflax potions",
"Toadflax potion (unfinished) are used to create Saradomin brews. Because these are often used to train Herblore, and adding clean toadflax to vials of water gives little experience, many players avoid the tedium of making unfinished potions and buy them directly from the Grand Exchange. This opens up an opportunity to make unfinished toadflax potions for profit.",
"Bank chest or other stationary banking location with a portable well placed next to it, use the \"Portables\" friends chat to find the current locations",
"making-weapon-poison.standard",
"Making weapon poison++",
"Money making guide/Making weapon poison++",
"Skavid map",
"Ring of duelling",
"Wearing any pair of gloves with an armour stat, such as: Gauntlets, Vambraces, or Leather gloves",
"Watchtower",
"Bullseye lantern (lit) optional to skip the warning dialogue on cave entry",
"Anachronia Dinosaur Farm: Perks",
"Coconut milk",
"Weapon poison++ is made by using cave nightshade on a vial of coconut milk and poison ivy berries. Cave nightshade only spawns inside the Skavid caves under Gu'Tanoth, east of Castle Wars, and is untradeable, so the spawn time of the nightshade is the limiting factor in how fast weapon poison++ can be made.",
"It takes approximately 30 seconds for each of the plants to respawn (with a small amount of randomness), and both caves contain 7 plants. You can gather more quickly by hopping world rather than waiting for respawns.",
"The varanusaur envenomed perk gives a 10% chance to make 4 doses instead of 3 doses when mixing these potions.",
"Skavid caves",
"making-yew-incense-sticks.standard",
"Making yew incense sticks",
"Money making guide/Making yew incense sticks",
"65 Firemaking",
"Yew incense sticks",
"An inventory of 28 Yew Logs can be crafted into 14 Yew incense sticks. This can be done at any bank. Setting a bank preset to be 28 Yew logs can make the banking process slightly easier. Players can simply buy yew logs at the Grand Exchange, process and resell the sticks. It takes 42 seconds to process 28 yew logs, so a full load of 2000 will take at least 3024 seconds, or 50 minutes.",
"mining-adamantite-ore.standard",
"Mining adamantite ore",
"Money making guide/Mining adamantite ore",
"40 Mining",
"Adamant pickaxe or better (recommended)",
"50 Mining (recommended)",
"Adamantite ore is an item that often sells for a high price, as it can be smelted in a furnace with a luminite ore to form an adamant bar, requiring level 40 Smithing.",
"There are several locations to mine adamantite, but one of the best places to mine adamantite is at the Rimmington mine (see page for banking details).",
"First, go to the ore locations and start mining. Once the player have a full inventory, go to the nearest bank, deposit the ores, return to the ore location, and repeat. The player may also find sedimentary geode while mining, which can increase the profit slightly. The player should also keep their stamina up, and mine any rockertunity the player may encounter, as it can increase the profit.",
"Mining luminite ore in the dwarven mines gives you more mining experience per hour and might be more profitable. Here's a table over experience gained and profit while mining luminite.",
"Varrock South-East mine",
"Use Archaeology journal teleport, then run west.",
"Use Varrock lodestone, then run east.",
"mining-animica.dark-animica",
"Tagga's corehammer gives the player +10% critical strike chance and +35 critical strike damage. It also has a 8.5% chance of producing deathspore arrow tips.",
"mining-animica.during-trahaearn-voice-of-seren",
"During Trahaearn Voice of Seren",
"Pickaxe of earth and song with Honed 6 and Refined 3",
"Dragon battleaxe (Legacy mode, special)",
"Grace of the elves (Seren spirits) with Luck of the Dwarves",
"Elder rune ore box",
"Rock-crushing scrimshaw",
"Light and Dark animica are high level tier 90 ores, used to make Elder rune bars.",
"When the hour begins, drink a sip of perfect juju mining potion, summon a lava titan, and if on legacy mode, use dragon battleaxe's special. You will want to find a world with two of the same rocks close to each other, so a rockertunity will spawn next to you. Click these for extra experience and more damage, meaning faster rocks. You can also 4 tick to keep your stamina up and mine faster.",
"If you do not have Grace of the elves or signs of the porter, a bank and a furnace are reasonably close. An elder rune box can initially hold up to 100 ore, and level 95 Mining and completion of the Everything Is Oresome achievement each increase the capacity by 20, up to a total maximum of 140 ore. Igneous and metamorphic geodes have a chance to appear in your inventory, while metamorphic geodes are quite rare, you can expect between 0-5 (4-5 rare) for 1 hour of mining animica.",
"Profit could be further increased with a Tagga's corehammer as it gives the player +10% critical strike chance and +35 critical strike damage, and also has a 8.5% chance of producing deathspore arrow tips.",
"Trahaearn runite mine, Prifddinas, during Trahaearn Voice of Seren",
"mining-animica.light-animica",
"UNDERGROUND_PASS",
"Underground Pass when mining at Lletya mine",
"When mining at Tumeken's remnant it is recommended to have protection against desert heat",
"This is an excellent way to mine fairly AFK for a long period of time, and the metamorphic geode does provide some additional income over time, but it is highly dependent on luck and having the Refined perk, alternatively you can use the Fortune perk to occasionally mine an extra ore. Stone spirit and ore prices fluctuate significantly on the Grand Exchange, so make sure to test them before investing in materials. For a close approximation of ore mined per hour (of pure mining) based on your levels and gear see the mining rate calculator.",
"Tagga's corehammer gives the player +10% critical strike chance and +35 critical strike damage, and also has a 8.5% chance of producing deathspore arrow tips.",
"mining-banite.standard",
"Mining banite",
"Money making guide/Mining banite",
"Pickaxe of earth and song with Honed 6",
"Shooting Star buff recommended",
"It is recommended to use the Wilderness (level 54) Pirates' Hideout mine as its close proximity to a metal bank negates the need for an ore box. Be sure to opt out of PvP as this location is in the deep Wilderness.",
"With level 99 Mining or above, the Mining cape gives a 5% chance to obtain double ore.",
"A grace of the elves allows Seren spirits to spawn, which reward the player with an item from the rare drop table. However, be aware that the grace of the elves has a high upfront cost as it becomes permanently untradeable once equipped for the first time.",
"Tagga's corehammer gives the player +10% critical strike chance and +35 critical strike damage. It also has a 6.2% chance of producing deathspore arrow tips.",
"Pirates' Hideout mine (level 54 Wilderness)",
"Using a Slayer cape or any of its variants to teleport to Mandrith, who is very close to the mine.",
"Use Wilderness sword 4 teleport to Wilderness Agility Course, then run northeast.",
"Use Pull the lever in East Ardougne or Edgeville to teleport to Deserted Keep, run north, then west.",
"Obelisk (Wilderness) to level 44 Wilderness, north through the gate, then northeast.",
"mining-clay.standard",
"Mining clay",
"Money making guide/Mining clay",
"Clay",
"Players can also use Bracelet of clay to further boost their hourly profit. Each bracelet will allow the player to mine 28 soft clay before disintegrating.",
"It takes around 40 seconds running to and from the bank. Depending on your mining level and pickaxe your profit will be a bit different. There will be no increased ore per hour after steel pickaxe. For a close approximation of ore mined per hour (of pure mining) based on your levels and gear see the mining rate calculator. You can see the differences in this table.",
"mining-common-gem-rocks-in-al-kharid-mine.standard",
"Mining common gem rocks in Al Kharid mine",
"Money making guide/Mining common gem rocks in Al Kharid mine",
"16 Mining for all gems included in this income table",
"99 Dungeoneering (recommended)",
"40 recommended for adamant or better pickaxe",
"Ring of kinship recommended or bank teleports",
"Dungeoneering master cape",
"Hoardstalker ring",
"Dungeoneering cape, Dungeoneering master cape or Hoardstalker ring (recommended)",
"Common gem rock",
"Uncut lapis lazuli",
"Assumes the guide's 1,400 actions per hour. Adjust it to your own pace.",
"Using the Dungeoneering cape, Dungeoneering master cape, or the Hoardstalker ring, teleport to Al Kharid resource dungeon, but do not enter the dungeon. Mine any one of several common gem rocks available. With a full inventory, teleport close to a bank, such as Edgeville lodestone, and repeat. Common gems are in demand for the creation of exquisite urns.",
"Mining rate can be checked using the calculator: Calculator:Mining/Rate.",
"Use the Dungeoneering cape, Dungeoneering master cape, or the Hoardstalker ring, teleport to Al Kharid resource dungeon, but do not enter the dungeon. Mine any one of several common gem rocks available. With a full inventory, teleport close to a bank, such as Edgeville lodestone, and repeat. Common gems are in demand for the creation of exquisite urns.",
"mining-concentrated-coal-rocks.standard",
"Mining concentrated coal rocks",
"Money making guide/Mining concentrated coal rocks",
"Steel ore box or better",
"Coal stone spirits",
"Ring of Wealth or better",
"Coal can be mined from concentrated coal deposits in the Living Rock Caverns. Unlike regular coal rocks, concentrated coal deposits yield five pieces of coal at once.",
"Note that the coal obtained in the above example requires 4-ticking. Afk methods will produce around 6000 ore.",
"It is recommended to use a lava titan, requiring 83 Summoning, to give an extra 10 mining damage to increase the speed at which the coal is mined. The golden mining suit gives a 5% increase to experience when worn, but it does not increase the rate that the coal is mined. A full decorated mining urn can be teleported for 625 mining experience, but it does not affect the rate of obtaining coal and it cannot be sold. For the purpose of money making, it is not recommended to use urns as they take up inventory space and provide no benefit to the amount of coal earned. For a close approximation of coal mined per hour (of pure mining) based on your levels and gear see the mining rate calculator.",
"Be sure to assign an action bar slot for your ore box if not using signs of the porter, to avoid wasting extra time depositing coal.",
"Once your inventory and your ore box is full, you'll need to run back towards the Pulley lift at the entrance of the Living Rock Caverns. Simply use your Orebox on the Pulley to deposit all of your ore, then click deposit on the Pulley and right click and deposit all of the ore in your inventory. Be careful when depositing your inventory of ore, not to deposit your Orebox.",
"mining-concentrated-gold-rocks.standard",
"Mining concentrated gold rocks",
"Money making guide/Mining concentrated gold rocks",
"Elder rune pickaxe + 5 or better",
"Gold stone spirit (recommended)",
"Note that the gold ore obtained in the above example requires 4-ticking. Afk methods will produce around 3780 ore.",
"It is recommended to use a lava titan, requiring 83 Summoning, to give an extra 10 mining damage to increase the speed at which the gold ore is mined. The golden mining suit gives a 5% increase to experience when worn, but it does not increase the rate that the gold ore is mined. A full decorated mining urn can be teleported for 625 mining experience, but it does not affect the rate of obtaining ore and it cannot be sold. For the purpose of money making, it is not recommended to use urns as they take up inventory space and provide no benefit to the amount of gold ore earned. For a close approximation of ore mined per hour (of pure mining) based on your levels and gear see the mining rate calculator.",
"Once your inventory and your ore box is full, you'll need to run back towards the Pulley lift at the entrance of the Living Rock Caverns. Simply use your Orebox on the Pulley to deposit all of your ore, then click deposit on the Pulley and right click and deposit all of the ore in your inventory. Be careful when depositing your inventory of ore, not to deposit your orebox.",
"mining-copper-ore.standard",
"Mining copper ore",
"Money making guide/Mining copper ore",
"Copper stone spirit",
"Mining tin ore can be done in several different places but one of the best is in the dwarven mines underneath Falador. The output is calculated having full stamina at all times. It should be noted that you will be getting sedimentary geodes while mining. The geodes can later be opened to retrieve spirit shards and different gems. The player should use the best pickaxe possible as it will grant more ores per hour (up to steel pickaxe). Below is a table of estimated profit per hour with different mining levels and pickaxes. For a close approximation of ore mined per hour (of pure mining) based on your levels and gear see the mining rate calculator.",
"mining-granite.standard",
"Mining granite",
"Money making guide/Mining granite",
"Crystal pickaxe or better",
"70 Mining (recommended)",
"Desert robes (recommended)",
"Granite (5kg)",
"Granite is an item in demand for its use as tertiary ingredient in making granite lobster pouches. It can be mined from granite rocks in the Desert Quarry. As the Desert Quarry is located far from a bank, collecting granite can be difficult. However a player can use a sign of the porter IV, or better, to send granite to their bank as it is mined. Signs of the porter are untradeable and must be created by the player. A sign of the porter IV is created from an emerald necklace and 45 vibrant energy. Players can use lower level signs of the porter, but, as lower level signs of the porter are able to send fewer items to the bank before being used up, they will be able to use this method for less time before needing to bank to get more signs of the porter. As granite can only be mined in the Kharidian desert, an enchanted water tiara or completion of Crocodile Tears is needed to avoid taking damage from the desert heat. Players may also wish to wear Varrock armour 2 or better to have a chance of mining two pieces of granite at once. Mining granite could be combined with cutting granite to make additional profit.",
"The Bandit Camp lodestone is a quick and free teleport, available after completing Desert Treasure. The quarry is a short run south west of the lodestone.",
"After completing Enakhra's Lament, players can use the Camulet to teleport to Enakhra's Temple, which is very near the quarry. The temple's western exit is perhaps the most convenient for granite mining. The Camulet is by a wide margin the quickest way to get to the quarry.",
"Players can use a Bandit Camp teleport scroll to teleport to the centre of the Bandit Camp and walk south to the quarry.",
"Players can use a Pharaoh's sceptre to teleport to Jaldraocht and walk west to the quarry.",
"Granite is an item in demand for its use as tertiary ingredient in making granite lobster pouches. It can be mined from granite rocks in the Desert Quarry. As the Desert Quarry is located far from a bank, collecting granite can be difficult. However a player can use a sign of the porter IV, or better, to send granite to their bank as it is mined. Signs of the porter are untradeable and must be created by the player. A sign of the porter IV is created from an emerald necklace and 45 vibrant energy. Players can use lower level signs of the porter, but, as lower level signs of the porter are able to send fewer items to the bank before being used up, they will be able to use this method for less time before needing to bank to get more signs of the porter. As granite can only be mined in the Kharidian desert, an enchanted water tiara or completion of Crocodile Tears is needed to avoid taking damage from the desert heat. Players may also wish to wear Varrock armour 2 or better to have a chance of mining two pieces of granite at once.",
