"Starting your run, fill your inventory and pack yak with muddy keys. Teleport to the level 44 obelisk using an obelisk shard or the portable obelisk. Make your way through the maze, slashing the webs apart and avoiding the hellhounds. Having a kitchen built in Fort Forinthry gives a 100% success rate in slashing spider webs. Reach the muddy chest at the end. Avoid the aggressive ripper demons inside the muddy chest area or turn on Protect from Melee/Deflect Melee. When finished, teleport out of the maze. Bank, heal if necessary, and refill your yak and inventory with keys using a preset. Rinse and repeat.",
"Be wary as your first used key can drop items on the floor. Dive and Mobile can be used to optimise your running time. Out of the three ripper demons at the end of the maze, only the westernmost one is in aggro range of the chest. The best way to deal with it is to lure it north, outside of the fence, then east and directly south, on top of the earth staff spawn.",
"Use Starting your run, fill your inventory and pack yak with muddy keys. Teleport to the level 44 obelisk using an obelisk shard or the portable obelisk. Make your way through the maze, slashing the webs apart and avoiding the hellhounds. Having a kitchen built in Fort Forinthry gives a 100% success rate in slashing spider webs. Reach the muddy chest at the end. Avoid the aggressive ripper demons inside the muddy chest area or turn on Protect from Melee/Deflect Melee. When finished, teleport out of the maze. Bank, heal if necessary, and refill your yak and inventory with keys using a preset. Rinse and repeat.",
