"operating-partial-potion-producer-dx.standard",
"Operating partial potion producer DX",
"Money making guide/Operating partial potion producer DX",
"114 Invention",
"Built a partial potion producer DX and fill it with charges",
"Can be done every 13 days 13 hours; a run takes about 2 minutes.",
"13 days 13 hours",
"Make sure you're actually using the partial potion producer DX, instead of the regular potion producer. If you do not, the profit gained from this activity will be lower than shown on this page. For more detailed information on which herb to select, see the §Potion prices section below.",
"Unfinished potions are always in high demand because of their use in the Herblore skill.",
"You will first need to have built a partial potion producer, then create the partial potion producer DX. You can build a partial potion producer DX in the Invention Guild with 114 Invention. If provided with machine charge, this machine will turn clean herbs and vials of water into their respective unfinished potion. It can hold up to 13,000 items at once, and can be left to run just short of two weeks without any required input.",
"With a jumbo generator, up to three partial potion producers DX can be run at a time, potentially resulting in tripled profit, at the expense of not being able to run any other type of machine. To allow profit to be easily calculated for any combination of machines, this page calculates profit on a per-machine basis.",
"The input capacity and processing time for each type of invention machine (alchemiser, potion producer, disassembler etc) varies. See below for examples.",
"operating-the-alchemiser-mk-ii.standard",
"Operating the Alchemiser mk. II",
"Money making guide/Operating the Alchemiser mk. II",
"108 Invention",
"Alchemiser mk. II",
"Can be done every 8 days 8 hours; a run takes about 2 minutes.",
"8 days 8 hours",
"Make sure you're actually using the alchemiser mk. II, instead of the regular alchemiser. If you do not, the profit gained from this activity will be lower than shown on this page as that machine also requires fire runes and processes fewer items every day. For more detailed information on which item to select, see the Item prices section below.",
"You will first need to have built a regular alchemiser, then create the alchemiser mk. II. You can build a alchemiser mk. II in the Invention Guild with 108 Invention. If provided with machine charge, this machine will cast the High level Alchemy spell on the provided items. The machine will alchemise 600 items daily. It can hold up to 5,000 items at once, and thus can be left to run just over 8 days without any required input.",
"It is possible to boost your Invention level with an extreme invention potion by 17 levels, allowing you to build the alchemiser Mk. II and a jumbo generator at level 91 Invention. Once you have boosted, you must go to the inventor's workbench and research the blueprint.",
"The buy limit for dragon items is either 10 every four hours (60 per day) or 100 every four hours (600 per day), depending on the item. As the alchemiser mk.",
"performing-powerful-essence-rituals.standard",
"Performing Powerful essence rituals",
"Money making guide/Performing Powerful essence rituals",
"At level 95 Necromancy, players can perform Powerful essence rituals to create Impure essence, an important ingredient used in Runecrafting Necrotic runes for Necromancy combat.",
"This is the number of rituals at which all glyphs will be fully used without leaving any on the ritual floor, assuming that ritual components are only repaired when they reach 0 durability.",
"Use After completing Rune Mythos and Requiem for a Dragon, use Ungael Teleport to reach the ritual site. To use the site after the quest, speak to the Archivist while wearing Zorgoth's ring.",
"Ungael Teleport",
"performing-greater-necroplasm-rituals.standard",
"Performing greater necroplasm rituals",
"Money making guide/Performing greater necroplasm rituals",
"Assumes the guide's 45 actions per hour. Adjust it to your own pace.",
"Responding to ritual disturbances will improve return on investment and experience rates, but will reduce the number of outputs.",
"This assumes six Multiply II glyphs are being used with a tier 3 ritual site (90 Necromancy, not boostable) for +240% output. Obtaining the Underworld Grimoire 2 grants another +5% output.",
"performing-lesser-necroplasm-rituals.free-to-play",
"5 Necromancy",
"performing-lesser-necroplasm-rituals.multiply-glyphs",
"Multiply glyphs",
"103 Necromancy (recommended)",
"This assumes eight Multiply III glyphs, an alteration necklace, the Necromancy cape attuned to Multiply III, and the Underworld Grimoire 4 are being used with a tier 3 ritual site (90 Necromancy, not boostable) for +663% output.",
"performing-manifest-ectoplasm-rituals.standard",
"Performing manifest ectoplasm rituals",
"Money making guide/Performing manifest ectoplasm rituals",
"Elite Morytania achievements",
"Ring of Kayazu (recommended)",
"Bucket of slime",
"At level 95 Necromancy, players can perform Manifest ectoplasm rituals to create ectoplasm, an important ingredient used in Necromancy combat. The limiting factor of this money making method is gathering buckets of slime, which are untradable. It is currently not possible to use the notepaper on the buckets, but you can use the bucket on the notepaper to convert the buckets into bank notes.",
"City of Um / ritual site",
"picking-cabbages.standard",
"Picking cabbages",
"Money making guide/Picking cabbages",
"Explorer's ring 3 or better",
"Low-level players should beware Goblin Raids spawning on the cabbage patch, although Goblin Raiders are not aggressive.",
"Falador Cabbage Patch, War's Retreat",
"picking-cadava-berries.standard",
"Picking cadava berries",
"Money making guide/Picking cadava berries",
"Cadava berries are valuable as ingredients in Necromancy potions. They can be picked from cadava bushes south of Varrock. There are 3 of them with 2 berries each, or 6 in total.",
"Due to the long respawn time, this method requires world switching to gather berries more quickly. The gathering speed would depend on how fast world switching can be done.",
"Cadava berries are in high demand and the bushes are not instanced, so there might be occasional competition making it take longer to gather berries.",
"South of Varrock",
"picking-coconuts.standard",
"Picking coconuts",
"Money making guide/Picking coconuts",
"Palm trees already planted in patches",
"Can be done every 270 minutes; a run takes about 5 minutes.",
"picking-curry-leaves.standard",
"Picking curry leaves",
"Money making guide/Picking curry leaves",
"Witchdoctor mask or Juju teleport spiritbag",
"Curry trees already planted in patches",
"Curry leaf",
"Curry leaves grow on curry trees, and they're used in Cooking and Farming. Once a curry tree has grown fully, it can be harvested repeatedly, with a curry leaf growing back every 45 minutes for a maximum of six.",
"picking-glowing-fungus.standard",
"Picking glowing fungus",
"Money making guide/Picking glowing fungus",
"Underworld Grimoire 1 or better",
"Picking up glowing fungus and dropping it turns it into ashes, highly valued for Necromancy as an ingredient of ghostly ink. The Underworld Grimoire is required as it automatically banks any ashes picked up and the glowing fungus is very remote. Once you have picked up a piece of the fungus, drag and drop it onto your action bar. Once it is bound to a key, you can hold that key indefinitely and any fungus you hold and further pick would automatically be dropped. Click the dropped ashes to open the loot interface, then you can use space to loot and bank all ashes on the ground at once. One inventory can be banked in about 36 seconds, or 100 loads in 1 hour (although you don't have to bank 28 ashes exactly every time). Glowing fungus regrows almost instantly.",
"There is no direct path to the mine; the fastest method to reach the entrance is to use a Games necklace or Drakan's medallion to teleport to Burgh de Rott and run west. Otherwise, players must travel through Mort Myre Swamp.",
"picking-papayas.standard",
"Picking papayas",
"Money making guide/Picking papayas",
"78 Summoning",
"Papaya trees already planted in patches",
"Papaya fruits grow on papaya trees, and they're used in Summoning, Hunter and Farming. Once a papaya tree has grown fully, it can be harvested repeatedly, with a papaya growing back every 45 minutes for a maximum of six.",
"picking-potatoes.standard",
"Picking potatoes",
"Money making guide/Picking potatoes",
"Raw potatoes are the base ingredient for all types of potatoes with toppings. There is a consistent demand for raw potatoes on the Grand Exchange, and someone has to pick them!",
"Pick the potatoes - travelling diagonally along the rows is most effective. Members can store potatoes in sacks to reduce the amount of time spent banking, and increase profit earned per hour. Potato seeds are sometimes obtained from picking potatoes on members worlds; it is therefore recommended to do this method on a free to play world.",
"Lumbridge potato field",
"picking-primal-fruit.standard",
"Picking primal fruit",
"Money making guide/Picking primal fruit",
"72 for Anachronia Teleport",
"Spirit tree re-rooter (3 charges consumed)",
"Plague's End for additional patches",
"The Jack of Spades for the Menaphos cactus patch",
"Completion of The Lute of Love for an additional fruit tree patch",
"The Prisoner of Glouphrie recommended for gnome gliders",
"Totem of the Abyss in the northern space recommended",
"LOVE_STORY",
"House in Rimmington or Love Story recommended",
"101 recommended (116 for maximum Farming XP, boostable)",
"92 recommended for Wolpertinger",
"Farming cape recommended for occasional instant harvesting and noting",
"Master farmer outfit recommended for additional yield",
"Easy Ardougne achievements recommended for a teleport",
"Bountiful Harvest upgrade recommended for additional yield",
"Spirit trees planted in Brimhaven and Etceteria recommended",
"Construct the additional cactus patches",
"Wolpertinger pouch",
"Carambola seed",
"Lychee seed",
"Lychee",
"Golden dragonfruit",
"Carambola",
"Can be done every 360 minutes (fruit and cactus regrow every 120 minutes); a run takes about 6 minutes.",
"360 minutes (fruit and cactus regrow every 120 minutes)",
"See also primal fruit pulp for info on fruit. Harvesting primal fruit allows a player to get farming XP while collecting valuable fruit. Once a plant has fully grown, fruit can be collected regularly without additional input. Higher level fruit gives more experience, more pulp and often more profit. The master farmer gives a 10% chance to get an additional piece of fruit at the bush or fruit tree patches. Unlocking Bountiful Harvest 2 from the Garden of Kharid gives a 7% chance of an additional item upon each harvest.",
"A primal fruit run consists of 3 parts.",
"For the bush patches a wolpertinger doubles yield and XP. The bush can be clicked once per tick for faster harvesting. The patches are at.",
"Champion's guild, reachable from the Combat bracelet or Varrock lodestone.",
"Rimmington, reachable from a (modified) Teleport to house or Port Sarim lodestone.",
"4 × cactus patches, 8 × fruit tree patches, 5 × bush patches",
"Use Champion's guild, reachable from the Combat bracelet or Varrock lodestone.",
"Use Rimmington, reachable from a (modified) Teleport to house or Port Sarim lodestone.",
"picking-up-eggs-at-fred-s-farm.standard",
"Picking up eggs at Fred's Farm",
"Money making guide/Picking up eggs at Fred's Farm",
"Chargebow or Staff of air",
"Pick up eggs at Fred's Farm. Once you enter the farm, close the gate behind you and kill all the chickens outside the gate using cheap ranged/magic weapons (such as a chargebow or air staff). Chickens will then only respawn and spawn eggs inside the gate. Stay at the centre of the farm, and area loot as eggs shows up. It is recommended to keybind area loot to make picking up eggs easier.",
"Fred's Farm",
