"Adamant dart tip",
"Although adamant dart tips can be smithed by a current free player, they must have previously completed The Tourist Trap, a members-only quest.",
"Although smithing adamant dart tips only requires level 40 Smithing, level 49 Smithing is recommended in order to create each unfinished smithing item with the highest possible heat available, maximising the number of dart tips smithed per hour.",
"smithing-cannonballs.double",
"Double",
"71 for double ammo mould",
"Double ammo mould added to the tool belt",
"The double ammo mould is a reward from the dwarven mines Thieving chest and doubles the production rate of smithing cannonballs.",
"smithing-cannonballs.regular",
"Ammo mould added to the tool belt",
"smithing-elder-rune-5-items.standard",
"Smithing elder rune + 5 items",
"Money making guide/Smithing elder rune + 5 items",
"Ancient elven ritual shard (if using Superheat Form)",
"Smithing autoheater",
"Advanced smithing autoheater",
"Smithing autoheater or Advanced smithing autoheater",
"99 Smithing (recommended)",
"76 recommended (boosted to 93) for 'Ancient tools' blueprint and perks",
"Grace of the elves recommended (if using Superheat Form)",
"Scroll of efficiency (recommended)",
"Smithing cape (recommended)",
"Hammer-tron",
"Enhanced hammer-tron",
"Augmented crystal hammer",
"Hammer-tron or Enhanced hammer-tron or Augmented crystal hammer recommended (augmented with Rapid 4 and Tinker 4 or similar)",
"95 optional for extreme invention potion for invention boost",
"It is highly recommended that the player is at least level 99 Smithing to do this method since the player can smith elder rune items 10% faster at level 99. It is also highly recommended to use the Superheat Form Seren prayer, as this allows smithing for longer before needing to reheat the item. If owned, wearing a grace of the elves halves the prayer point drain of Superheat Form. (While having high requirements, equipping an Orthen furnace core will stop Superheat Form from draining prayer at all.) Players can use ancient elven ritual shard and/or super prayer renewals to restore prayer points.",
"Players being on World 70 with active luminite injectors also helps increase the amount produced per hour.",
"Players can gain 6% more experience with the full blacksmith's outfit.",
"Players can receive the benefits of Varrock armour 4 without wearing the armour by completing the easy New Varrock achievements.",
"Players can gain Artisans' Workshop respect while doing this method.",
"Artisans' Workshop (highly recommended) or anywhere with an anvil",
"smithing-elder-rune-shields.standard",
"Smithing elder rune shields",
"Money making guide/Smithing elder rune shields",
"Elder rune round shield",
"If owned, it is recommended to use an orthen furnace core and Superheat Form to maintain high heat and produce shields faster. This requires completion of The Light Within and level 99 Smithing and 102 Archaeology to create the orthen furnace core. In one hour you can make about 32-33 shields using this method.",
"smithing-glorious-bars.standard",
"Smithing glorious bars",
"Money making guide/Smithing glorious bars",
"Smelting gauntlets (recommended)",
"Create 50 concentrated alloy bars using 1 of each of the bars listed above per alloy bar.",
"Use the concentrated alloy bars to create 10 enriched alloy bars.",
"Use the enriched alloy bars to create 1 immaculate alloy bar.",
"Start folding the immaculate alloy bar into a glorious bar. A partially folded alloy bar must be folded 1,001 times to produce. It takes about 2,004 ticks, or 20 minutes, to produce one glorious bar.",
"smithing-rune-arrowheads.standard",
"Smithing rune arrowheads",
"Money making guide/Smithing rune arrowheads",
"Although smithing rune arrowheads only requires level 50 Smithing, level 59 Smithing is recommended in order to create each unfinished smithing item with the highest possible heat available, maximising the number of arrowheads smithed per hour.",
"smithing-rune-bolts-unf.standard",
"Smithing rune bolts (unf)",
"Money making guide/Smithing rune bolts (unf)",
"Although smithing rune bolts (unf) only requires level 50 Smithing, level 59 Smithing is recommended in order to create each unfinished smithing item with the highest possible heat available, maximising the number of bolts smithed per hour.",
"smithing-rune-dart-tips.standard",
"Smithing rune dart tips",
"Money making guide/Smithing rune dart tips",
"Rune dart tip",
"While rune dart tips can be smithed by a current free player, they must have previously completed The Tourist Trap, a members-only quest.",
"Although smithing rune dart tips only requires level 50 Smithing, level 59 Smithing is recommended in order to create each unfinished smithing item with the highest possible heat available, maximising the number of dart tips smithed per hour.",
"Any location with an anvil.",
"smithing-rune-knives.standard",
"Smithing rune knives",
"Money making guide/Smithing rune knives",
"Although smithing rune knives only requires level 50 Smithing, level 59 Smithing is recommended in order to create each unfinished smithing item with the highest possible heat available, maximising the number of knives smithed per hour.",
"smithing-steel-nails.standard",
"Smithing steel nails",
"Money making guide/Smithing steel nails",
"Steel nails",
"Although smithing steel nails only requires level 20 Smithing, level 28 Smithing is recommended in order to create each unfinished smithing item with the highest possible heat available, maximising the number of nails smithed per hour.",
"spinning-flax.spin-flax-spell",
"Spin Flax spell",
"81 Magic",
"Lunar spells activated",
"It is highly recommended that you make a bank preset with 25 flax, 5 astral runes, and 10 nature runes.",
"spinning-flax.spinning-wheel",
"Spinning wheel",
"The best method for free-to-play players is to use the spinning wheel on the floor 1 above ground of Lumbridge Castle, and to bank on the floor 2 above ground. You should use a preset with flax in your inventory to speed up the process. Alternative, if you pick the flax yourself in Taverly, use the spinning wheel just north, near Jack Oval and bank in Burthorpe.",
"In members the closest spinning wheel to a bank is in Neitiznot, which requires completion of The Fremennik Isles to access. Another good option is Seers' Village if you have completed the medium Seers' Village achievements. You can then equip the Seer's headband 2, which has the benefit of spinning the flax 33% faster. If the Ranger's Workroom is constructed in Fort Forinthry, this unlocks a spinning wheel with a bank chest right beside it.",
"spinning-starbloom-flowers-into-cloth.standard",
"Spinning starbloom flowers into cloth",
"Money making guide/Spinning starbloom flowers into cloth",
"100 Crafting",
"Starbloom cloth",
"First, spin starbloom flower into starbloom thread at a spinning wheel.",
"The spinning wheel in the Ranger's Workroom (at least tier 1) in Fort Forinthry is right next to a bank, so it's an optimal location for this.",
"Next, weave starbloom thread into starbloom cloth at any loom.",
"Both starbloom thread and starbloom cloth are stackable, so it's wise to process all of your starbloom flower into starbloom thread first, and then process all of that starbloom thread into starbloom cloth at once.",
"Ranger's Workroom spinning wheel, Fort Forinthry",
"spinning-wool.standard",
"Spinning wool",
"Money making guide/Spinning wool",
"1,000,000+ coins recommended",
"Assumes the guide's 50 actions per hour. Adjust it to your own pace.",
"The best possible method is to use the spinning wheel on the floor 1 above ground of Lumbridge Castle, and to bank on the floor 2 above ground. A full load of 28 wool takes approximately 50 seconds to convert into balls of wool. Travel and banking time is ~20 seconds in between loads. You should use a preset with wool in your inventory to speed up the process.",
"stealing-cave-goblin-wire.standard",
"Stealing cave goblin wire",
"Money making guide/Stealing cave goblin wire",
"44 Thieving",
"DEATH_TO_THE_DORGESHUUN",
"Death to the Dorgeshuun",
"Cave goblin wire",
"Players may enter the crack in the eastern wall of the cellar of Lumbridge Castle, through which Kazgar waits to lead players through the Dorgesh-Kaan mine. The entrance to Dorgesh-Kaan is just to the south-east of where Kazgar leaves the player. To follow Kazgar through the mines, the player is required to bring a light source.",
"The city can be accessed from the Kalphite Hive through the Dorgesh-Kaan South Dungeon to the south of the city, although a light source is required.",
"There is a fairy ring in the dungeon to the south with the code AJQ. This may only be used if players have completed A Fairy Tale II - Cure a Queen up to the point where the fairy ring network is unlocked. A light source is needed in the dungeon. To exit from the dungeon to the city, go east of the ring, then go north, west and again to north until a ladder. Climb up the ladder to the Dorgesh-Kaan course, and climb down the stairs to the north to reach the southern part of the city.",
"The Dorgesh-Kaan–Keldagrim train system may be used to travel to Dorgesh-Kaan from Keldagrim by rail (after Another Slice of H.A.M.), and vice versa. The tickets are free; a player need only wait less than a minute in the carriage for the departure. The train station in Keldagrim is located near the blast furnace in the south-east of the city, and the train station in Dorgesh-Kaan is on the floor 1 above ground in the south-west corner of the city.",
"stealing-from-vegetable-stalls.standard",
"Stealing from vegetable stalls",
"Money making guide/Stealing from vegetable stalls",
"2 Thieving",
"Garlic",
"stringing-magic-longbows.standard",
"Stringing magic longbows",
